      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 137, \"items_by_type\": {\"table\": [{\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy table: one row per department/lab/center (DLC) under the 'Standard Hierarchy' hierarchy type, recording the DLC key/code/name and its five-level hierarchy path from the institute root (level 1 'All Departments') through executive areas down to the DLC's placement, with each level's code and name (null for levels deeper than the DLC's position). Joins to HR_ORG_UNIT and FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY; used to report or filter the master-hierarchy placement (school/area path) of a DLC, and as a DLC scope filter when only DLCs present in the standard hierarchy should be included.\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with unit key/ID/title, unit level classification (ALL MIT, TOP LEVEL, DEPARTMENTS, SUB DEPARTMENT, ORGANIZATION LEVEL, NON HIERARCHY ORG UNITS), HR department identifiers and name variants (short, long, alphabetical), organization hierarchy area names (school area, top level, root), the full HR hierarchy path levels 1-7 (each with ID, sort order, and name), and DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME cross-references to departments/labs/centers. Joined from FCLT_ORGANIZATION and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY to attach HR department attributes (title, level, department name, long name, hierarchy path) to facilities organizations and DLCs; a single DLC_KEY can map to multiple HR org unit rows, so joins via DLC_KEY may fan out.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization dimension table: one row per organization in the institute's hierarchical organization tree (levels 1-6, from institute-wide down to sub-units), with organization identifiers and names, parent and major-organization attribution, hierarchy level, assignable-space flag, course number for academic departments, description, DLC (department/lab/center) key and name, and cross-references to HR organization units. Parent of SPACE_UNIT (space assigned to organizations) and referenced by FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY for room occupancy attribution.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization snapshot table with the same hierarchical organization structure as FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization identifiers, parent/major organization, level, assignable flag, course number, description, HR cross-references) but keyed by ORGANIZATION_KEY and carrying D_CODE instead of DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME. Contains fewer organizations than FCLT_ORGANIZATION; used as an alternative organization dimension in FAC_* family queries.\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy link table: one row per association between a department/lab/center (DLC) and a linked administrative object, classified by link type (Standard Funds Center, PCMIT-0 Profit Center, New/Old Org. Unit, Facilities Org., Student Systems Unit, NIMBUS B.A.G.). A DLC may hold many links of several types. Joins to MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY; used to map DLCs to their fund centers, profit centers, facilities organizations, and other linked object codes.\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT\", \"desc\": \"Department parent lookup table: one row per department code (D_CODE) with its department name and the identity of its direct parent department (parent ID, parent D code, parent name). A flattened single-level parent view of the department tree; use MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY when the full multi-level hierarchy path of a DLC is required. D_CODE matches MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY/DLC_CODE and other DLC key columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW\", \"desc\": \"Newer HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with the same unit/department identity and hierarchy-path structure as HR_ORG_UNIT (unit key/ID/title/level, HR department code and name variants, school-area/top-level/root names, hierarchy path levels 1-5, DLC_KEY) but a shallower hierarchy path (levels 6-7 absent), no HR_DEPARTMENT_ID and no DLC_NAME column, and an extra HR_DEPARTMENT_ABBR abbreviation column. Holds more unit rows than HR_ORG_UNIT (691 vs 641, including units absent from HR_ORG_UNIT); use HR_ORG_UNIT when DLC_NAME or the deeper hierarchy path is required, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW for the newer unit coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"FUND_CENTER_HIERARCHY\", \"desc\": \"24 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"Space unit dimension table: one row per space unit (an organizational space-assignment unit such as a department, program, or office that receives space allocation), with space unit key/code, space unit name, the facilities organization it belongs to, and DLC key. Bridges FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization attribution) and SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to the space unit); used to group room counts and space statistics by space unit.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_FLOOR\", \"desc\": \"Facilities floor inventory table: one row per floor of a building (floor key formatted '<building key>-<floor>'), with floor number/label, gross, assignable and non-assignable areas of the floor, sort sequence, level identifier, building wing, and access level. Child of FCLT_BUILDING via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY and parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_FLOOR_KEY; used for per-floor area aggregation and floor-level filtering (e.g. floors with assignable area above a threshold).\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_FACULTY_ROSTER\", \"desc\": \"HR faculty roster table: one row per faculty member keyed by MIT_ID with name components, terminal degree, appointment type, job/position titles across HR, administrative, and directory organization units, endowed chair, and emeritus status. Used for faculty appointment and credential analysis; joins to EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY on MIT_ID for contact details.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"SIS department dimension table: academic departments with code, name, full name, school attribution (code and name), budget code, degree-granting flag, and commencement-book names. Joins to subject offering tables via department codes.\"}, {\"id\": \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"Student-facing department lookup table with department code, name, full name, and school attribution (code and name). Similar in content to SIS_DEPARTMENT but oriented to student information systems reporting; joins to offering tables via DEPARTMENT_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"SIS administrative department table with administrative department code/name, phone area code and phone number, and clearing cost collector. Joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT via SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE for department contact information.\"}, {\"id\": \"DRUPAL_EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY\", \"desc\": \"Drupal-sourced employee directory table: an alternative employee feed keyed by MIT_ID with name components, employee group/type, additional/dual appointment flags, office location and phone, HR organization unit id/title, directory/primary titles, email address, and personal URL. Same person domain as EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY but from the Drupal source system and without Kerberos/preferred-name columns; used as an alternative employee lookup when Drupal-sourced attributes (employee group, appointment flags, HR org unit) are needed.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_FLOOR\", \"desc\": \"Facilities floor snapshot table (FAC_* family): one row per floor of a building with floor number/label, gross, assignable and non-assignable areas, sort sequence, level, wing, and access level. Same floor structure as FCLT_FLOOR but keyed by FLOOR_KEY/BUILDING_KEY joining FAC_ROOMS.FLOOR_KEY and FAC_BUILDING.FAC_BUILDING_KEY; used as the floor source when FAC_* family keys are involved.\"}, {\"id\": \"SE_PERSON\", \"desc\": \"Person master table keyed by MIT_ID with Kerberos name, full name, payroll rank, position title, active flag, office location, organization, name components, and employee type. A general-purpose person dimension covering employees with payroll/position attributes; narrower contact information than EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY (no email or phone).\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY\", \"desc\": \"Bridge table mapping facilities organizations to their department/lab/center (DLC) keys: one row per organization-DLC key assignment. Used to filter organizations that have a non-null DLC key assignment before joining FCLT_ORGANIZATION (via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY or DLC_KEY) for DLC-level facility and room statistics.\"}, {\"id\": \"EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY\", \"desc\": \"Employee directory table: one row per institute employee with MIT ID, legal and preferred name components, directory/primary titles, HR department number and name, office location and office phone, email address, personal URL, and Kerberos name. Used to resolve responsible faculty contact details (full name, email, office phone) for subject offerings via RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID = MIT_ID, and to link employees to Moira mailing list membership via MIT_ID = MOIRA_LIST_MEMBER_MIT_ID.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_UNIT2\", \"desc\": \"Alternative space unit lookup table containing space unit key, code, name, and DLC key, but without the FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY organization attribution present in SPACE_UNIT. Holds fewer space units than SPACE_UNIT; used when only space unit identity/name is needed without organization linkage.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level rollup of section offerings per term: one row per subject offered in a term with unit structure (total/lecture/lab/preparation units), offering department and school, responsible faculty, cluster information, and enrollment numbers. Parent of SUBJECT_OFFERED (section level) via COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Section-level subject offering fact table: one row per subject section offered in a term, with section flags (master/lecture/lab/recitation/design), cluster information, offering department and school, responsible faculty, meeting time/place, and enrollment numbers at section, subject, and cluster level. Linked to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (subject level) via SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY/COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY and to SUBJECT_SUMMARY via SUBJECT_SUMMARY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_FLOOR_HIST\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities floor table: one row per floor per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format, covering 201505-201602), preserving each floor's number/label, gross, assignable and non-assignable areas, sort sequence, level, wing, and access level over time. Fiscal-period counterpart of FCLT_FLOOR; joins to buildings via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY and to current floor records via FCLT_FLOOR_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_ROOMS\", \"desc\": \"Facilities room snapshot table with the same room inventory structure as FCLT_ROOMS (building/floor keys, room identifiers, major/minor use classifications, organization assignment, area, access level, coordinates) but keyed by FAC_ROOM_KEY and joining the FAC_* family (FAC_BUILDING, FAC_FLOOR, FAC_ORGANIZATION). Used as an alternative room source when FAC_* family keys are involved.\"}, {\"id\": \"MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY\", \"desc\": \"Student directory table: one row per student with name components, full name, office location and phone, email address, department code and department name, and student year. The DEPARTMENT column stores the academic department code and joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, enabling per-department student counts.\"}, {\"id\": \"ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD\", \"desc\": \"Space-planning room load table: one row per room record from the space planning feed, with the building-room identifier, building component, floor (numeric or label such as 'G9'), space usage text (e.g. 'DSGN STUDIO', 'CONF RM'), space unit code, HR organization unit id, and room access level. Links rooms to SPACE_UNIT via SPACE_UNIT_CODE and to FCLT_ORGANIZATION/HR_ORG_UNIT via HR_ORG_UNIT_ID; used for floor/access-level/space-usage room analysis from the space-planning perspective, without the area and use-key columns carried by FCLT_ROOMS.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\", \"desc\": \"SIS course description table: catalog descriptions of courses with department and school attribution, course level (undergraduate/graduate), degree-granting flag, graduate level, CIP program code, and effective from/thru terms. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via COURSE = SUBJECT_CODE/COURSE_NUMBER and to SIS_DEPARTMENT via DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"ROLES_FIN_PA\", \"desc\": \"2 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_BUILDING\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building snapshot table (FAC_* family): one row per physical building with the same building attribute structure as FCLT_BUILDING (number/name, type, ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates, site, coordinates) but keyed by FAC_BUILDING_KEY and joining the FAC_* family (FAC_ROOMS, FAC_FLOOR, FAC_BUILDING_ADDRESS, FAC_ORGANIZATION). Used as the building dimension when FAC_* family keys are involved; FCLT_BUILDING is the counterpart in the FCLT_* family.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building inventory table: one row per physical building with building number/name, type (e.g. ACADEMIC), ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates (built/acquired/occupied), site and geographic coordinates. Parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ROOMS\", \"desc\": \"Facilities room inventory table: one row per physical room with building/floor keys, room identifiers, use classifications (major/minor use), organization assignment, area in square meters, access level, and geographic coordinates. Joins to FCLT_BUILDING via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY; referenced by COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.MEET_PLACE via FCLT_ROOM_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION_HIST\", \"desc\": \"22 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_PERSON\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject person table: one row per person associated with an IAP activity, recording the person's role in the activity (Activity leader, Session leader, Contact person), MIT affiliation type, name, location, email, organization, and title. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_PERSON_KEY; used to analyze activity leadership and person roles, e.g. enrollment capacity statistics per person role.\"}, {\"id\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Course catalog subject offering table recording catalog-level attributes of each subject offered per academic year and term: subject identity (SUBJECT_ID = SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_NUMBER), department, unit structure (lecture/lab/preparation/design/total units), grading type and rules, HGN level (Undergraduate/Graduate/High Graduate), requirement attributes (GIR, HASS, communication, writing), term offering flags (this year, fall, IAP, spring, summer), instructors, section flags, responsible faculty, and meeting time/place. Links to terms via both TERM_CODE (the offering term) and EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE (the term from which catalog attributes take effect).\"}, {\"id\": \"OPA_PERSON_CURRENT\", \"desc\": \"Current-person snapshot table from the OPA (Office of People Analytics) feed: one row per current person keyed by MIT_ID with name components, email, HR job attributes (job id/title, admin employee type, HR department, org unit and position titles, payroll rank), faculty flag, employment percent, privacy flags, sabbatical begin/end dates, and personnel subarea. Used for HR/appointment analysis of current people; carries no office phone or office location.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE\", \"desc\": \"Space supervisor usage fact table: one row per supervisor (MIT_ID) recording how much space they supervise and for how many departments: department count, department DLC key list (comma-separated when multiple), number of supervisees, supervised square footage, research volume, and derived ratio measures (sqft per supervisee, sqft per research volume, research volume per sqft). Joins to SPACE_UNIT and other DLC-carrying tables via DEPT_NAMES = DLC_KEY (only single-department rows match); used for supervisor space-usage and research-volume statistics per department/DLC.\"}, {\"id\": \"LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR\", \"desc\": \"Library course instructor table recording instructors of courses with library reserve materials, including course name, instructor name, department (in 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' format), assignment date range, and library organizational unit/branch. Referenced by LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL via LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR_KEY; instructor names resolve to person records via INSTRUCTOR_NAME = SE_PERSON.FULL_NAME.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Space assignment detail fact table: one row per physical room assigned to a space unit, with building/floor/space-unit/space-usage keys, room identifiers (building-room number and name, room number), room square footage, room counter, and building component. Used to count rooms per space unit or per building, and to analyze room size and usage distribution. Joins to SPACE_UNIT via SPACE_UNIT_KEY, FCLT_BUILDING via BUILDING_KEY, SPACE_FLOOR via FLOOR_KEY, and SPACE_USAGE via SPACE_USAGE_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_CATEGORY\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject category lookup table with category name and description. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_CATEGORY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level summary fact table per term: one row per subject (or cluster) per term with department/school attribution, unit structure (total/lecture/lab/prep/design units), and detailed enrollment statistics including final enrollment, first-week and fifth-week enrollment, and credit/listener splits at both subject and cluster level. Used for enrollment and unit statistics by department, school, term, and subject group.\"}, {\"id\": \"BUILDINGS\", \"desc\": \"Space-domain building lookup table: one row per building with building key/number, building name, street and mailing addresses as single text fields, gross and assignable square footage (in square feet), and a building counter. Referenced by SPACE_DETAIL via BUILDING_KEY; a lightweight building reference for space-assignment reporting, without the type/ownership/site classification carried by FCLT_BUILDING or FAC_BUILDING.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_MAJOR_USE\", \"desc\": \"Facilities major use classification lookup table (FAC family): same major use code/description/assignable structure as FCLT_MAJOR_USE but keyed by MAJOR_USE_KEY and joining the FAC_* family (FAC_ROOMS.MAJOR_USE_KEY). Used as the major use decoder when FAC_ROOMS is the room source.\"}, {\"id\": \"TOP_LEVEL_DOMAIN\", \"desc\": \"4 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_MAJOR_USE\", \"desc\": \"Facilities major use classification lookup table (FCLT family): one row per major use code (e.g. CLASSRMS classrooms, OFFICES offices, LABS laboratories, RESIDENT residential) with its short code, description, and assignable-space flag. Joined from FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_MAJOR_USE_KEY to decode a room's major use; current snapshot only, use FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST for fiscal-period historical variants.\"}, {\"id\": \"CIP\", \"desc\": \"Classification of Instructional Programs (CIP) lookup table: one row per six-digit CIP program code, classifying instructional programs into a two-digit category and a four-digit series, with program/category/four-digit titles, a change note, the CIP revision version year (1990/2000/2010/2020), and the warehouse load date. Joins to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION via PROGRAM_CODE = CIP_PROGRAM_CODE to attribute courses to CIP programs, categories, and schools/departments; CIP_WITH_VERSION is the multi-version variant keeping every revision of each program code.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ROOMS_HIST\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities room table: one row per room per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format; current data covers period 201505), preserving each room's identifiers, floor, use classifications, organization assignment, area, access level, and coordinates over time. Fiscal-period counterpart of FCLT_ROOMS; joins to current room records via FCLT_ROOM_KEY and to buildings via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"CIS_COURSE_CATALOG\", \"desc\": \"CIS course catalog table: an alternative course catalog source with the same subject attribute structure as COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (units, grading, requirement attributes, offering flags), keyed by academic year, term code, and subject identity. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via DEPARTMENT_CODE for subject code resolution.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_GROUPING\", \"desc\": \"7 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Library subject offered table: subjects offered per term that appear in library reserve processing, with subject identity, course number, offering department/school, responsible faculty, and enrollment count. Parent of LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL via LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"TIME_DAY\", \"desc\": \"Day-level time dimension table mapping each calendar date to fiscal year/period, calendar year/period, academic year, financial aid year, day of week, and the academic term code/description the day belongs to. Used to attach calendar attributes to terms and activities.\"}], \"metric\": [{\"id\": \"dw_4773\", \"desc\": \"For each organization with an organization level of 5 and for rooms on floor 2 that are associated via space unit code, show the organization name, organization key, description, space unit, space unit key, the average organization key within each organization key group ordered by space unit key, the building room, space usage, the HR org unit title, the department name, the minimum access level in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the building component, and the HR org unit level and department code for each room, ordered by organization name and building room. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4033\", \"desc\": \"For rooms on floor 2, show the building room, space usage, the organization name, the HR org unit title, the department name, the minimum access level in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the building component, the department's long name, the DLC name, and the highest floor among rooms with access level 1 for each space usage group. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3692\", \"desc\": \"For each organization and department in the Provost Area with a non-null department code, where the organization level is 5 and assignable is 1, show the organization name, organization key, department name, department code, the average organization key within each organization key group ordered by department code, the department's long name, the corresponding hierarchy level 3 name from the master department hierarchy, and the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the department name. The columns should be shown in the following order: organization name, organization key, department name, department code, the average organization key window value, department's long name, hierarchy level 3 name, and the department hierarchy row number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4590\", \"desc\": \"For organizations with an organization level of 5, show the organization name, organization ID, DLC name, HR org unit title, HR department name, HR org unit level, and assign row numbers within each HR department name group ordered by organization name. For each such organization, for each room with area greater than 200 and assignable major use, show the building room, floor, room number, space ID, area, major use name, major use description, and the minimum area value over each major use group. Additionally, for each such room, show the HR org unit title and HR org unit level from the HR_ORG_UNIT table (joined via DLC_KEY), and the difference between the room's area and the minimum area for its major use. Order the results by HR department name, organization name, and major use. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4627\", \"desc\": \"For organizations with an organization level of 5, show the organization name, organization ID, DLC name, HR org unit title, HR department name, HR org unit level, and assign row numbers within each HR department name group ordered by organization name. For each such organization, for each room with area greater than 200 and assignable major use that belongs to the organization, show the building room, floor, room number, space ID, area, major use name, major use description, and the minimum area value over each major use group. Additionally, for each such room, show the HR org unit title and HR org unit level from the HR_ORG_UNIT table (joined via DLC_KEY). Present the results with the columns: organization name, organization ID, DLC name, HR org unit title, HR department name, HR org unit level, row number, building room, floor, room number, space ID, area, major use name, major use description, minimum area per major use, HR org unit title (from HR_ORG_UNIT), and HR org unit level (from HR_ORG_UNIT), in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4025\", \"desc\": \"For rooms with a square footage of 150, show the space unit code, space unit name, and the maximum rank within each space unit code group, and for each of those space units, show the major organization, top-level HR organization name, HR department name, the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the organization numbers for each HR department name, considering only organizations that are assignable and have a non-null organization number. The results should include the space unit code, space unit name, maximum rank, major organization, top-level HR organization name, HR department name, average organization number, organization number variance, and organization number standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3452\", \"desc\": \"For organizations with an organization level of 5 and departments in the \\\"Provost Area\\\" with a non-null department code, show the organization name, organization ID, DLC name, HR org unit title, HR department name, HR org unit level, the row number within each HR department name group ordered by organization name, the department's long name, the corresponding hierarchy level 3 name from the master department hierarchy, and the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the department name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4271\", \"desc\": \"For rooms on floor 2 with access level 1, show the space unit, the maximum row number (within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by building room) for each space unit, the building room, the organization name, the department name, and the difference between the access level of the room and the average access level for that department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1864\", \"desc\": \"For each organization whose organization level is 5 and is not 'ADMISSIONS', and for each organization and its corresponding HR department where the organization is assignable, the HR organization unit level is 'DEPARTMENTS', the organization is not 'Cambridge-MIT Institute', and the organization is in the 'Provost Area' top-level HR hierarchy, but excluding organizations with organization IDs '138' and '250', show the organization name, description, the corresponding space unit name, the total number of space units associated with each organization, the HR department name, the number of organizations, and the minimum organization number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2559\", \"desc\": \"For each DLC whose DLC name contains the word 'Office', is not the biology department, and has at least one assignable organization, what are the DLC key, DLC name, the number of unique organizations, the total number of assignable organizations, the department name, the maximum organization number, the name of the space unit associated with that department, and the earliest warehouse load date among its organizations, considering only departments in the \\\"Provost Area\\\" with a maximum organization number greater than 50000 and excluding the \\\"Political Science\\\" department (Course 17)? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3890\", \"desc\": \"For each major use description, list the building-room identifier, area, major use description, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the major use description, as well as the organization name, department name, department code, department long name, department level, and the average organization number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the organization parent, ordered by the organization name, but only include those organizations whose organization number is greater than the average organization number of their parent group. For each major use description, include a grand total row for all rooms in the format of (null, null, major use description, total rooms) and only include rooms whose organization matches the filtered organizations. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3235\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and its corresponding facility organization key where the department is in the Provost Area, provide the number of organizations, the minimum department hierarchy level 3 code, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of HR organization units per facility organization (considering only those with a non-null DLC key and where the hierarchy type is 'Standard Hierarchy'), listing the results in order by department name and facility organization key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4330\", \"desc\": \"For each organization that is assignable and has a department code above 100000, and for which there exists a space unit with space unit code equal to 97500, show the organization key, organization name, department name, the number of HR org units, the total of their department IDs, the latest warehouse load date from HR_ORG_UNIT, the space unit name, the DLC name, the DLC key from the organization, the minimum space unit code in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the facility organization key, and the total number of space units per organization, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3919\", \"desc\": \"For departments in the \\\"Sloan School of Management\\\" area with a hierarchy type of \\\"Standard Hierarchy\\\", show the department code, department name, the dense rank of each department considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the department's long name, and the corresponding DLC name from the MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY table, along with, for each such department, the space unit code, organization name, HR department name from the space unit, the sum of space unit keys within each warehouse load date group, and the HR org unit title for space units with a space unit key greater than 100000, where the department and space unit share the same DLC key. Present the results in the order of department code and space unit code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3490\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the \\\"Provost Area\\\" with a non-null department code, show the department name, the department's long name, the corresponding hierarchy level 3 name from the master department hierarchy, the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the department name, and for each matching space unit with a space unit key greater than 100000, show the space unit code, the organization name, the HR department name from the space unit, and the sum of space unit keys within each warehouse load date group ordered by space unit key. Present the results ordered by department name and space unit code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3904\", \"desc\": \"For each subject code where the department is degree granting, show the subject code, subject code description, department name (from subject code), school name, the number of subject codes per school name and whether the subject code description is present ('Has Description') or missing ('No Description'), and for each matching department in subjects offered in the term with code '2022SU', show the subject's ID, total units, department name (from subject offered), and their dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the total number of units. For each school name, include a grand total for all subject codes in the format of (null, null, null, school name, null, total subject codes, null, null, null, null). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3916\", \"desc\": \"For each warehouse load date, list the space unit code, organization name, HR department name, the HR org unit title, the sum of space unit keys within each warehouse load date group (including a grand total row with nulls and the total sum), and for each, show the building room, space usage, space unit name, and the total number of rooms in the same space unit on floor 2 with access level 1 (only including space units with more than 1 such room), for space units with a space unit key greater than 100000. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3299\", \"desc\": \"For rooms with an access level of 1 in building E38, show the building-room identifier, the area, the major use description, the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the major use description (for access level 1 rooms), the floor number, the major use description, the organization name, the office location, the full name of the employee, the department name, and the average area of rooms in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by department number and ordered by floor. List the columns in the following order: building-room identifier, area, major use description, access level window row number, floor number, major use description, organization name, office location, full name of the employee, department name, and average area window. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4776\", \"desc\": \"For rooms with an area greater than 300 that are associated with departments in the \\\"Provost Area\\\", show the building-room identifier, floor number, major use description, organization name, DLC key, the average area in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by department code and ordered by area, the department code, department name, school area name, and the rank of each department within its school area based on department code. Additionally, include the department's full name from the HR organization unit and the department's hierarchy level 3 name from the master department hierarchy. Present the results ordered by building-room identifier and department code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4562\", \"desc\": \"For each organization with an organization level of 5 whose space unit is among the top 10 space units by number of rooms, display the organization name, organization key, description, space unit, space unit key, the average organization key within each organization key group ordered by space unit key, the count of rooms for each space unit, and the building with the highest number of rooms in that space unit, along with the count of rooms in that building. Order the results by the count of rooms descending and then by space unit key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3342\", \"desc\": \"For each space unit with a space unit key greater than 100000 that is associated with a department in the \\\"Provost Area\\\", show the space unit code, the organization name, the HR department name, the sum of space unit keys within each warehouse load date group, the HR department code, the school area name, and the rank of the department within its school area based on department code. Present the results ordered by school area name, department rank within school area, and space unit code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3153\", \"desc\": \"Among all organizations with a DLC key of 'D_MECHE' and an organization level of 5, what are the names and descriptions of these organizations, and for each, what is the name and description of their parent organization? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4612\", \"desc\": \"For each organization whose parent is 'S H&SS' and that is associated with a space unit with space unit code 97500, list the organization name, description, HR org unit title, row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the organization name, the space unit name, space unit code, department count, number of supervisees, the average department count within each department count group ordered by number of supervisees, and the total square footage for each organization. Include subtotals for each organization (the corresponding organization name field is 'SUBTOTAL') and a grand total across all organizations (the corresponding organization name field is 'TOTAL'). Do not repeat the organization name if it is the same as the previous row. Sort the table by organization name and space unit name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2896\", \"desc\": \"For each facility organization, show the research volume, department names, square footage, MIT ID, and the average square footage in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows (grouped by facility organization key and ordered by research volume) for space supervisor usage records where the number of supervisees is 2, and only include those records where the average square footage in the window is greater than 200. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3215\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2012, show the subject key, subject title, offer department name, academic year, term description, the row number within each offer department name group ordered by subject key, the subject code, subject code description, department name, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the school code and ordered by school code, for subjects where the school code is not null and the subject title is not null. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3277\", \"desc\": \"List all subject titles that are either (a) offered in the term '2022FA' with a total of 12 units, showing the subject title, department name from the course description, and the dense rank of each subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the subject code from the course catalog, or (b) for each subject offered, show the subject title, subject ID, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject key. The results should include all these columns in the following order: subject title, department name, window column, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and maximum number of enrolled students, with NULLs for columns not relevant to each case. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1350\", \"desc\": \"For each department and school, provide the department name, school name, the average, range, and variance of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department, and the total enrolled students, considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with at least one enrolled student. Additionally, for each school, include a grand total for all departments in that school in the format of (null department name, school name, nulls for statistics, and total enrolled students). For students whose first name is 'Peter' and who are in the Mathematics department, also show their last name, email address, student year, and the minimum department budget code in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the student's full name, as well as the department full name and department last activity date. The results include all these columns in the following order: department name, school name, average enrolled students, range of enrolled students, variance of enrolled students, total enrolled students, last name, email address, student year, windowed minimum department budget code, department full name, and department last activity date. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1357\", \"desc\": \"For each access level code and campus sector, what is the access level code, access level name, campus sector, the variance of the number of rooms in the building history for buildings with a nonzero number of rooms, assignable area greater than 0, and that are residential buildings at MIT, as well as, for each floor in the Fairchild Building with access level 1 or 2 and in academic buildings, the floor number, the building's long name, the range and variance of the area of rooms on that floor? Only include buildings that are at MIT. Also, include subtotals for each access level code (the corresponding campus sector field is 'SUBTOTAL') and a grand total across all access level codes (the corresponding campus sector field is 'TOTAL'). Do not repeat the access level code if it is the same as the previous row. Sort the table by access level code, campus sector, and floor. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4405\", \"desc\": \"For each combination of activity and department/academic year enrollment statistics, list the activity title, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, category name, category description, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the category name and ordered by the category name, along with the department name, academic year, number of unique subjects offered (subject count), minimum number of total units for those subjects, and the average number of enrolled students per subject (for departments and academic years where the number of enrolled students in a subject is greater than 5). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4452\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the \\\"Provost Area\\\" that is associated with a space unit with space unit code 97500, show the department code, department name, school area name, the rank of each department within its school area based on department code, the corresponding DLC name, the space unit name, space unit code, associated organization name, department count, number of supervisees, and the highest research volume ever recorded for each department count group. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1488\", \"desc\": \"For each academic building at MIT and each of its floors with total assignable area greater than 5000 and at least one room with access level 1 or 2, provide the building's long name, the floor number, the range and variance of the area of rooms on that floor (considering only rooms with access level 1 or 2), the range and variance of the assignable area of its floors that have at least one room, and the total number of rooms in the building. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3828\", \"desc\": \"For courses in the School of Engineering that are degree granting, show the course description, department name, the dense rank of each course considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the department's budget code, the subject code description, and the row number of each course within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by course description. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3901\", \"desc\": \"For each offer department code in the 2012SU term with total units greater than 0, list the subject title, course number, department name, the dense rank over the offer department code, the course, course description, school name, program code, program title, category code, category title, four digit code, four digit title, and the minimum warehouse load date from the CIP table over each category code group for courses in department 6, and include a grand total of subjects per offer department code and a grand total for all courses in each school in the format (nulls for subject-specific fields, department name, total subjects, course-specific fields, school name, and total courses). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2151\", \"desc\": \"For each department that grants degrees (excluding the Biology department), provide the department name, the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year, and, if the department is Political Science, also include for each HGN code the maximum number of lecture units among all subjects in the course catalog and the subject title from the subject offered table for subjects offered in the year 2012 with more than 2 lecture units, as well as the number of enrolled students for those subjects. List the results ordered by the variance of total units in descending order, and for Political Science, by the maximum lecture units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3867\", \"desc\": \"For each subject in a department where the school code and subject title are not null, and for each subject offered in the 2022FA term with total units greater than the average for that term, display the subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, the number of subjects in the same department, the subject ID, the term description, and the running sum of total units for that academic year, ordered by subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_76\", \"desc\": \"For all buildings on the MIT site that are academic buildings with more than 50 rooms (according to the building history) and are specifically the Ray and Maria Stata Center, list each floor's number, the total assignable area on that floor, and the total non-assignable area, ordered by floor number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3498\", \"desc\": \"List all subject IDs that are either offered in the term with code '2025FA' or are offered in the term '2016SP' by departments that grant degrees, along with the subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, term start date, term end date, term parameter, the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department, and the dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the total number of units. For subjects from the term '2025FA', show the subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, term start date, term end date, term parameter, and the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department; for subjects from the term '2016SP' by degree-granting departments, show the dense rank as window_column. The results are ordered by subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3294\", \"desc\": \"For courses in the School of Engineering that are degree granting, and for academic term parameters where the term indicator is 'C', show the course description, department name, the dense rank of each course considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the department's budget code, the term parameter, the term code, the academic year, and the running sum of academic years within each department ordered by academic year, for cases where the department matches in both sets. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_5103\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2017JA', show the subject title, the number of enrolled students, the responsible faculty name, the offering department name, the department full name, the school name, and the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the department code. Additionally, for subjects offered in the term with code '2022FA' in the same department, provide the subject ID, department name, term description, the running sum of total units within each academic year ordered by subject ID, and the subject's short title and responsible faculty name from the course catalog. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1427\", \"desc\": \"For each course in the Mathematics department that is degree granting and has a course level of 'G', show the course description, department name, school name, the administrative department name, and the dense rank over the administrative department name ordered by the administrative department name. Additionally, for each administrative department name, include a grand total of the number of such courses in the format of (null, null, null, administrative department name, null, total courses). Also, show the minimum total units, the sum of lecture units, and the number of unique subjects for letter graded Mathematics department subjects offered in the Spring Term 2021, along with the department name and term description (with all other columns as null). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3861\", \"desc\": \"For subject offerings in the term '2017FA' with a total number of units greater than 10, display the subject title, department name, school name, and their dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the department code from the subject code table, along with any matching subject IDs from subjects offered in the term with code '2022SU', their department names, and their dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the total number of units. Show the subject title, department name, school name, subq1 dense rank, subject ID, subq2 department name, and subq2 dense rank, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4184\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the offer department name, the number of distinct subjects offered by the department in the academic year 2012, and for each subject that was offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", display the subject key, subject title, academic year, term description, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, and the deviation of each subject's enrollment number from the average enrollment number for its subject key group, ordered by offer department name and subject key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1833\", \"desc\": \"For each department and subject grade type where the subject is offered in the current academic year, is letter graded, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the number of subjects, the minimum total units, the school name, the department phone number, the organization name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the areas of its rooms, and the department's DLC name, including subtotals for each department (the corresponding department field is 'SUBTOTAL') and a grand total across all departments (the corresponding department field is 'TOTAL'). Do not repeat the department if it is the same as the previous row. Only include organizations that have more than 5 rooms, are associated with a non-null DLC key, and are not the 'ADMISSIONS' department or the 'Political Science' department. Sort the table by department, grade type, and descending standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of room areas. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1165\", \"desc\": \"For each subject where the responsible faculty MIT ID in the library subject offered table is 928034000 or the number of enrolled students in the tip subject offered table is greater than 5, and where the offer department name in the tip subject offered table is either 'Chemistry' or 'Biology', show the subject title from the library subject offered table, the offer department name from the tip subject offered table, the term code from both tables, the number of enrolled students from both tables, and the minimum number of enrolled students in the tip subject offered table over each master subject ID group. Additionally, for the department offering the subject, show the department name, the range of enrolled students, and the variance of enrolled students in the subjects offered by that department, considering only departments that grant degrees, courses that are at the graduate level, and excluding the Biology department. Present the results ordered by subject title and department name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3590\", \"desc\": \"Show, for each subject, the subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the school code and ordered by school code for subjects where the school code is not null and the subject title is not null; and for subjects offered in the 2012SU term with a cluster type of 'S', show the subject title from SUBJECT_OFFERED, the offer department name, the total units from SUBJECT_SUMMARY, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the subject title. Indicate the source of each row as either 'Subq1' or 'Subq2'. List all results together, showing the columns: subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, dense rank by school, offer department name, total units, row number window, and source, in that order, ordered by subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1465\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the Provost Area at the School of Science level, excluding the Biology department, and for each organization within those departments (excluding organizations with IDs '138' and '250'), show the department name, department code, organization name, organization ID, the maximum average organization number within each department code group, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the area of rooms assigned to the organization (considering only organizations with more than 5 rooms and excluding organizations named 'ADMISSIONS'), ordered by department name and organization name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4197\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the term with term code '2012SU' that also has a cluster type of 'S', show the subject title, offer department name, offer school name, cluster type description, the difference between the number of enrolled students for that subject and the average number of enrolled students for all subjects in the same department in that term, the dense rank of each subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the number of enrolled students, and the deviation of the number of enrolled students from the average number of enrolled students for that department in that term as calculated from the summary table. The columns should be shown in the following order: subject title, offer department name, offer school name, cluster type description, deviation from department average (from the first calculation), window column (dense rank), and deviation from department average (from the summary calculation). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4812\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 combinations of department name, subject code, and course number (where the department is degree granting and the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2) with the highest number of unique library subjects offered, display the department name, subject code, number of subject codes, minimum department budget code, course number, number of unique library subjects offered, minimum total units, the subject title with the most enrolled students for that course, and the corresponding number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3311\", \"desc\": \"For each course that has more than 0 enrolled students and a material status key of 'U', list the course number, course number description, number of enrolled students, reserve catalog key, and the dense rank over the material status key ordered by material status key, along with the department name, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units of courses offered by that department (considering only courses offered this year with non-null total units). Present the results ordered by course number and course number description. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1393\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year and department in Mathematics, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in that year and department (considering only subjects offered in the current term, with more than 0 total units, and with subject enrollment number greater than the average for that department and year), and for those departments, what are the department code, corresponding administrative department name, the graduate level of courses, and the total number of distinct courses per department, for all degree-granting departments except the Management department? Present the results as academic year, department name, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, administrative department name, graduate level, and number of distinct courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}], \"concept\": [{\"id\": \"concept_dept_hr_org_hierarchy\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing the institute's department/lab/center (DLC) and HR organization hierarchies: the HR organization unit dimension in two feed variants (HR_ORG_UNIT, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW), the master department standard hierarchy path (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY), its DLC-to-administrative-object link table (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS), and the direct-parent department lookup (MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT). They jointly answer questions about which HR department/area a DLC or organization belongs to, the hierarchy path or parent of a department, and HR department names/codes/levels, and are joined to FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY for facilities/space attribution. They differ in hierarchy representation (full path vs direct parent vs HR unit attributes), unit coverage, and companion columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_facility_organization_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Organization dimension tables describing the institute's hierarchical organization tree used for facilities/space attribution: FCLT_ORGANIZATION (keyed by FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, with DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME) and FAC_ORGANIZATION (keyed by ORGANIZATION_KEY, with D_CODE). They answer the same questions about organization names, hierarchy levels, parent/major organizations, assignable flags, and HR cross-references, but belong to different table families and coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_department_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables describing academic departments and their school attribution: the SIS department dimension, the student-facing department lookup, and the SIS administrative department (contact information). They answer questions about department names, full names, school code/name, degree-granting status, budget codes, and department phone numbers, but differ in attribute coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_space_unit_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Space unit lookup tables identifying the organizational units that receive space allocation: SPACE_UNIT (with FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY organization attribution) and SPACE_UNIT2 (identity/name only). They answer the same space-unit identity questions but differ in organization linkage and coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_person_directory\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing people of the institute keyed by MIT_ID: the primary employee directory (contact details, titles, HR department), the Drupal-sourced employee feed (employee group/type, appointment flags, HR org unit), the person master table (payroll rank, position title, active flag), the HR faculty roster (appointment type, terminal degree, emeritus status), the OPA current-person snapshot (HR job/appointment attributes, faculty flag, sabbatical), and the student directory (students with department attribution and student year). They jointly answer questions about who a person is, their contact details, job/appointment attributes, and whether they are employee, faculty, or student; responsible faculty in subject offering tables resolve to these tables via RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID = MIT_ID.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_room_space_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical room inventory and its space assignment: SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to space units with usage classification and square footage), FCLT_ROOMS (facilities room inventory with use classifications, organization assignment, and area in square meters), FAC_ROOMS (the FAC_* family room snapshot with the same structure as FCLT_ROOMS but FAC_* keys), and ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD (space-planning room load feed with floor, space usage text, access level, and space unit code / HR org unit id links). They jointly answer questions about how many rooms exist, room sizes, room usage, and which organization/space unit occupies rooms, but differ in assignment perspective, key family, and area units.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_floor_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the floor level of buildings: the current FCLT_* family floor inventory with floor areas, the FAC_* family floor snapshot with the same structure, the fiscal-period historical floor table, and the lightweight space-domain floor lookup. They jointly answer questions about floor numbers and per-floor assignable/non-assignable areas, but differ in time coverage, table family, and attribute richness.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_catalog_sources\", \"desc\": \"Tables providing catalog-level subject attributes (titles, unit structure, grading rules, HGN level, requirement attributes, offering-term flags) from different source systems: the warehouse course catalog, the CIS course catalog feed, and the Drupal course catalog feed. They answer the same catalog-attribute questions but differ in source system, extra columns, and join paths to department/subject-code lookups.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_room_major_use_classification\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables classifying rooms by major use (classrooms, offices, laboratories, residential, circulation, etc.) with a short code, description, and assignable-space flag. They cover the current classification in the FCLT and FAC table families and the fiscal-period historical classification in the FCLT family, jointly answering questions about what a room is primarily used for and whether that use counts as assignable space.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_building_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical building inventory and its attributes (number/name, type, ownership, site, campus sector, access level, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates): the current FCLT_* family snapshot, its fiscal-period history (in two date-format variants), the FAC_* family snapshot, and the lightweight space-domain building lookup. They jointly answer questions about building characteristics, areas, and room counts, but differ in time coverage, table family, attribute richness, and area units.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_subject_offering_facts\", \"desc\": \"Fact tables recording subjects offered per term from different business processes: the course catalog (planned catalog attributes), the registrar's section/subject offering records (actual sections and enrollment), subject-level summaries (final enrollment statistics), the textbook information program (subjects tracked for course materials), and library reserve processing (subjects with library reserve activity). They share subject identity (SUBJECT_ID, TERM_CODE) and department attribution but differ in granularity, enrollment semantics, and available measures.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_cip_program_classification\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables of the Classification of Instructional Programs (CIP) used to classify courses/instructional programs into two-digit categories, four-digit series, and six-digit program codes, with revision version years (1990/2000/2010/2020). CIP holds the current single-version classification (one row per program code, with a change NOTE), while CIP_WITH_VERSION preserves every revision of each program code across versions. Both join to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION via PROGRAM_CODE = CIP_PROGRAM_CODE to attribute courses to CIP programs and categories.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_time_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Time dimension tables of the warehouse at three granularities: TIME_DAY (one row per calendar date, with fiscal/calendar year and period, academic year, financial aid year, day of week, and the academic term code/description of the day), TIME_MONTH (one row per fiscal period in YYYYMM format, covering fiscal years 1996-2035, with fiscal quarter, calendar month, academic term, and financial aid year mappings), and TIME_QUARTER (one row per fiscal quarter, covering fiscal years 2000-2035, with quarter dates, payroll certification deadlines, and quarter status flags). They jointly answer questions about when fiscal periods/quarters/days run, which fiscal/calendar/academic year a date or month belongs to, and how day-level records roll up to months and quarters. They link to each other via FISCAL_PERIOD (day-month), FY_QUARTER_CODE (month-quarter), and FISCAL_YEAR (month-quarter association within the same fiscal year, fanning out months across all quarters of the year), and to the academic term tables via TIME_DAY.ACADEMIC_TERM_CODE or TIME_MONTH.ACADEMIC_TERM = TERM_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_moira_mailing_lists\", \"desc\": \"Tables of the Moira mailing-list/group domain: the list master (one row per list with name, description, active flag, and type flags such as mailing list, group, NFS group, public, hidden), the membership detail (one row per list member with member login, full name, MIT ID, and last update date), and the owner lookup (one row per owner entity with owner name and owner type LIST/USER/KERBEROS). They jointly answer questions about which lists exist and their properties, who belongs to a list, and who owns a list; MOIRA_LIST is the parent of MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL via MOIRA_LIST_KEY, and MOIRA_LIST_OWNER is referenced by MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL via MOIRA_LIST_OWNER_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_academic_term_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing academic terms and their calendar/status attributes. They jointly answer questions about when terms run, which academic/financial-aid/degree year a term belongs to, and whether a term is current, previous, future, or regular. Coverage differs: the full historical term list, the status-tracked term subset, and the three-row relative term parameter reference.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_iap_activities\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing Independent Activities Period (IAP) activities offered in January terms: activity details (title, enrollment type, max enrollment, fee, cancellation flags), sessions (location, date, times), sponsors (name, type), categories, and persons. They jointly answer questions about IAP activity counts, enrollment capacity, fees, session scheduling, and sponsorship.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_material_programs\", \"desc\": \"Tables covering course material provisioning: the Textbook Information Program (TIP) tracking textbook adoption status per subject offering, and library reserve processing tracking catalog items placed on reserve for subjects. They jointly answer questions about which subjects have course materials/textbooks, material status (TIP statuses such as 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options; library statuses such as 'U' Unknown, 'Y' Required Course Material), ISBNs, record counts, and reserve catalog item attributes. The two programs are linked by SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_building_address\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the postal/street addresses of buildings: the current FCLT_* family address table (multiple purpose-typed address rows per building), its fiscal-period historical counterpart, the FAC_* family address snapshot, and the single-text address fields of the space-domain BUILDINGS lookup. They jointly answer questions about where a building is located (street number/name, city, state, postal code), but differ in time coverage, address decomposition, and table family.\"}], \"column_concept\": [{\"id\": \"column_concept_department_name\", \"desc\": \"Department name columns across subject offering, catalog, lookup, employee, and library reserve instructor tables. Two academic naming conventions exist (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME) with the same academic value domain; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT also holds academic departments but in a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME shares the column name but holds the HR organizational unit name (different value domain). Choosing the right one depends on the table family, the value format, whether the department is the catalog owner or the actual offering department, and whether an academic or HR department is meant.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_dlc_key\", \"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key columns (values like 'D_AEROASTRO', 'D_IDSS', 'D_BIOLOGY') identifying a DLC across the facilities, HR, space, and academic-department domains. They are the universal cross-domain join key linking facilities organizations and space units to HR organization units, the master department hierarchy, and academic departments. Naming and completeness vary: DLC_KEY in most tables, D_CODE in MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT, DLC_CODE in the master hierarchy tables; some columns carry composite values ('D_DSL:HQ') or nulls.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_facility_organization_key\", \"desc\": \"Facility organization key columns attributing space units and rooms to organizations in the hierarchical organization tree. Two naming conventions exist across table families (FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY in FCLT_*/SPACE_* tables vs ORGANIZATION_KEY in FAC_* tables) with the same value domain.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_access_level\", \"desc\": \"Access level columns recorded at three granularity levels of the facilities domain plus the space-planning room feed: building-level ACCESS_LEVEL_CODE/ACCESS_LEVEL_NAME (current and per-fiscal-period history), floor-level ACCESS_LEVEL, and room-level ACCESS_LEVEL (FCLT_ROOMS, FAC_ROOMS, ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD). They share a numeric value domain (observed 0-3) but describe the access restriction of different physical objects or come from different feeds, so filters and joins must target the granularity and table family the question refers to.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_assignable_area\", \"desc\": \"Assignable-area measure columns at different granularity levels and time semantics: building-level current and per-fiscal-period assignable area, floor-level assignable area, and the space-domain assignable square footage. All FCLT_*/FAC_* columns are in square meters; BUILDINGS.BLDG_ASSIGNABLE_SQUARE_FOOTAGE is in square feet. Choosing the right column determines whether the measure is a building total, a floor total, a historical value, or a space-assignment figure.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_office_location\", \"desc\": \"OFFICE_LOCATION columns recording where a person's office/desk is, replicated across the person-directory tables (SE_PERSON, MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY, EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY, DRUPAL_EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY). All hold a building or building-room text identifier in the same value domain as FCLT_ROOMS.BUILDING_ROOM, but they describe different populations (employee/person master vs student vs primary employee directory vs Drupal employee feed) and differ sharply in non-null coverage and in how many values are building-room ('BLDG-ROOM') versus building-only ('BLDG'). Choosing the right column determines whose office is reported and whether room-level joins to FCLT_ROOMS succeed.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_space_unit_key\", \"desc\": \"Space unit key columns identifying the organizational space-assignment unit across the space dimension and fact tables. SPACE_UNIT_KEY is the join key linking SPACE_DETAIL room rows to space unit identity (name/code) and, through SPACE_UNIT, to the owning facilities organization.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_room\", \"desc\": \"Combined building-room identifier columns (e.g. '1-080') appearing in both the space assignment fact table and the facilities room inventory. They identify the same physical room concept but come from different business processes with different coverage and companion measures.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_master_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Master subject identifier columns (MASTER_SUBJECT_ID and its sortable variant MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT) replicated across the registrar offering tables, the subject summary, the textbook program, the library reserve program, and the CIS course catalog. For clustered subjects (e.g. joint or cross-listed offerings), the master subject identifier points to the leading subject of the cluster, so joining on it matches offerings that share the same master subject even when their own SUBJECT_ID differs. SUBJECT_ID/SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the subject itself, while MASTER_SUBJECT_ID/MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the cluster's master; the _SORT columns are the sortable forms of the same values used for cross-table joins.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_type_site\", \"desc\": \"Building classification columns replicated across the current and historical building tables of both table families: BUILDING_TYPE ('ACADEMIC', 'SERVICE', 'RESIDENT') and SITE ('MIT', 'BATES', 'LINC', 'BOS', etc.). They carry the same value domain but differ in time semantics: the building-table columns are the current classification, while the history-table columns are the classification recorded at each fiscal period, so filtering by one versus the other can select different building sets.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_year_columns\", \"desc\": \"Year columns across term, catalog, and time dimension tables representing different year systems: academic year, fiscal year, financial aid year, and degree year. Selecting the correct year system is essential for yearly grouping and partitioning.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Subject identifier columns shared across catalog, registrar, textbook-program, and library tables. SUBJECT_ID is the cross-domain subject join key in 'CODE.NUMBER' format (e.g. '18.01'); it appears in every subject-related fact table but at different grains and program scopes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_hass_attribute\", \"desc\": \"HASS (Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences) attribute code and description columns. The code columns appear in the three course catalog feeds and in the CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE lookup; description columns exist in three variants: the catalog-embedded HASS_ATTRIBUTE_DESC, the lookup's DESCRIPTION_ON_FORM (registration-form wording), and DESCRIPTION_IN_BULLETIN (short bulletin wording). Selecting the right description variant depends on the wording requested by the question.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_material_status_key\", \"desc\": \"Material status key columns of the textbook program (TIP) and library reserve program. Both are coded status references decoded by their own lookup tables (key value equals code value), with independent value domains: TIP statuses ('RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options, 'RC' Recommended, 'PC' Val-u option, 'BR' Bookstore recommends, 'CL' Go to class first, 'NM' Course has no materials, 'U' Unknown, plus NULL-description keys) vs library reserve statuses ('U' Unknown, 'R' null description, 'N' Non-Required Course Material, 'O' Reserve only, 'X' No Required Textbook, 'Y' Required Course Material).\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_term_code\", \"desc\": \"Term code columns in YYYYTT format (e.g. '2025FA', '2019SP', '2021JA', '2012SU'; TT = FA Fall, SP Spring, JA January/IAP, SU Summer) appearing across term dimension and fact tables. They are the universal join key linking subject offerings, textbook materials, library reserves, and IAP activities to term attributes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_fiscal_period\", \"desc\": \"Fiscal period code columns in YYYYMM format (e.g. '199602' = FY1996 period 2, '201505') appearing in two distinct roles: as the primary key of the month-grain time dimension (TIME_MONTH.FISCAL_PERIOD, also mirrored in TIME_DAY.FISCAL_PERIOD for day-to-month linkage), and as the snapshot-period stamp of the facilities historical tables (FCLT_BUILDING_HIST, FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1, FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS_HIST, FCLT_FLOOR_HIST, FCLT_ROOMS_HIST, FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST). Both roles share the same YYYYMM value domain, but the time dimension uses it for calendar grouping while the history tables use it to mark when a facilities snapshot was taken.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_enrollment_measures\", \"desc\": \"Enrollment measure columns across subject offering, summary, textbook-program, and library tables. Two families exist: NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (student headcount snapshots) and SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (official registrar enrollment), at section, subject, or program scope.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_num_of_rooms\", \"desc\": \"NUM_OF_ROOMS columns recording how many rooms a building contains, replicated across the current and historical building tables of both families. The building-table columns hold the current room count (one value per building); the history-table columns hold the room count at each fiscal period, used for room-count statistics (average, range, variance, minimum) across a building's history records.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_total_units\", \"desc\": \"Total credit unit columns replicated across catalog and registrar subject tables. They represent the same business quantity (total credit units of a subject) but come from different processes and pair with different companion unit columns.\"}]}}"
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_78132096c2114936a247dc54",
      "name": "semantic_search",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 137, \"items_by_type\": {\"table\": [{\"id\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION_HIST\", \"desc\": \"22 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization snapshot table with the same hierarchical organization structure as FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization identifiers, parent/major organization, level, assignable flag, course number, description, HR cross-references) but keyed by ORGANIZATION_KEY and carrying D_CODE instead of DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME. Contains fewer organizations than FCLT_ORGANIZATION; used as an alternative organization dimension in FAC_* family queries.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY\", \"desc\": \"Bridge table mapping facilities organizations to their department/lab/center (DLC) keys: one row per organization-DLC key assignment. Used to filter organizations that have a non-null DLC key assignment before joining FCLT_ORGANIZATION (via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY or DLC_KEY) for DLC-level facility and room statistics.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization dimension table: one row per organization in the institute's hierarchical organization tree (levels 1-6, from institute-wide down to sub-units), with organization identifiers and names, parent and major-organization attribution, hierarchy level, assignable-space flag, course number for academic departments, description, DLC (department/lab/center) key and name, and cross-references to HR organization units. Parent of SPACE_UNIT (space assigned to organizations) and referenced by FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY for room occupancy attribution.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_BUILDING\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building snapshot table (FAC_* family): one row per physical building with the same building attribute structure as FCLT_BUILDING (number/name, type, ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates, site, coordinates) but keyed by FAC_BUILDING_KEY and joining the FAC_* family (FAC_ROOMS, FAC_FLOOR, FAC_BUILDING_ADDRESS, FAC_ORGANIZATION). Used as the building dimension when FAC_* family keys are involved; FCLT_BUILDING is the counterpart in the FCLT_* family.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_ROOMS\", \"desc\": \"Facilities room snapshot table with the same room inventory structure as FCLT_ROOMS (building/floor keys, room identifiers, major/minor use classifications, organization assignment, area, access level, coordinates) but keyed by FAC_ROOM_KEY and joining the FAC_* family (FAC_BUILDING, FAC_FLOOR, FAC_ORGANIZATION). Used as an alternative room source when FAC_* family keys are involved.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_MAJOR_USE\", \"desc\": \"Facilities major use classification lookup table (FCLT family): one row per major use code (e.g. CLASSRMS classrooms, OFFICES offices, LABS laboratories, RESIDENT residential) with its short code, description, and assignable-space flag. Joined from FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_MAJOR_USE_KEY to decode a room's major use; current snapshot only, use FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST for fiscal-period historical variants.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_FLOOR\", \"desc\": \"Facilities floor inventory table: one row per floor of a building (floor key formatted '<building key>-<floor>'), with floor number/label, gross, assignable and non-assignable areas of the floor, sort sequence, level identifier, building wing, and access level. Child of FCLT_BUILDING via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY and parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_FLOOR_KEY; used for per-floor area aggregation and floor-level filtering (e.g. floors with assignable area above a threshold).\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_UNIT2\", \"desc\": \"Alternative space unit lookup table containing space unit key, code, name, and DLC key, but without the FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY organization attribution present in SPACE_UNIT. Holds fewer space units than SPACE_UNIT; used when only space unit identity/name is needed without organization linkage.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ROOMS_HIST\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities room table: one row per room per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format; current data covers period 201505), preserving each room's identifiers, floor, use classifications, organization assignment, area, access level, and coordinates over time. Fiscal-period counterpart of FCLT_ROOMS; joins to current room records via FCLT_ROOM_KEY and to buildings via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1\", \"desc\": \"Variant of the historical facilities building snapshot table with the same structure, keys, and coverage as FCLT_BUILDING_HIST (one row per building per fiscal period, FISCAL_PERIOD 201505-201906), differing only in date-column formatting: DATE_BUILT/DATE_ACQUIRED/DATE_OCCUPIED are stored as DD-MON-YY strings (e.g. '25-APR-03') instead of MM/DD/YYYY. Use FCLT_BUILDING_HIST for building history analysis unless the DD-MON-YY date representation is specifically required.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building address table: one row per address record of a building (a building may hold several addresses for different purposes such as street, mail, parcel, and E911 emergency addresses), with street number and suffix, directional prefixes/suffixes, street name and suffix, city, state, postal code, address purpose, city identifier, and E911 flag. Joins to FCLT_BUILDING via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY; used to locate buildings by city/state/street and to report address attributes alongside building characteristics.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building inventory table: one row per physical building with building number/name, type (e.g. ACADEMIC), ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates (built/acquired/occupied), site and geographic coordinates. Parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ROOMS\", \"desc\": \"Facilities room inventory table: one row per physical room with building/floor keys, room identifiers, use classifications (major/minor use), organization assignment, area in square meters, access level, and geographic coordinates. Joins to FCLT_BUILDING via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY; referenced by COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.MEET_PLACE via FCLT_ROOM_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS_HIST\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities building address table: one row per building address record per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format), preserving each address's street number/name/suffix, directionals, city, state, postal code, address purpose, and E911 flag over time. Fiscal-period counterpart of FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS; joins to buildings via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY and to current address records via FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_FLOOR_HIST\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities floor table: one row per floor per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format, covering 201505-201602), preserving each floor's number/label, gross, assignable and non-assignable areas, sort sequence, level, wing, and access level over time. Fiscal-period counterpart of FCLT_FLOOR; joins to buildings via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY and to current floor records via FCLT_FLOOR_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities major use classification table: one row per major use code per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD, e.g. 201505), preserving the code/description/assignable values of each classification across fiscal periods. Superset of FCLT_MAJOR_USE along the time dimension; use FCLT_MAJOR_USE for the current classification and this table when a specific fiscal period's classification is required.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"Space unit dimension table: one row per space unit (an organizational space-assignment unit such as a department, program, or office that receives space allocation), with space unit key/code, space unit name, the facilities organization it belongs to, and DLC key. Bridges FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization attribution) and SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to the space unit); used to group room counts and space statistics by space unit.\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with unit key/ID/title, unit level classification (ALL MIT, TOP LEVEL, DEPARTMENTS, SUB DEPARTMENT, ORGANIZATION LEVEL, NON HIERARCHY ORG UNITS), HR department identifiers and name variants (short, long, alphabetical), organization hierarchy area names (school area, top level, root), the full HR hierarchy path levels 1-7 (each with ID, sort order, and name), and DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME cross-references to departments/labs/centers. Joined from FCLT_ORGANIZATION and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY to attach HR department attributes (title, level, department name, long name, hierarchy path) to facilities organizations and DLCs; a single DLC_KEY can map to multiple HR org unit rows, so joins via DLC_KEY may fan out.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_MAJOR_USE\", \"desc\": \"Facilities major use classification lookup table (FAC family): same major use code/description/assignable structure as FCLT_MAJOR_USE but keyed by MAJOR_USE_KEY and joining the FAC_* family (FAC_ROOMS.MAJOR_USE_KEY). Used as the major use decoder when FAC_ROOMS is the room source.\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy table: one row per department/lab/center (DLC) under the 'Standard Hierarchy' hierarchy type, recording the DLC key/code/name and its five-level hierarchy path from the institute root (level 1 'All Departments') through executive areas down to the DLC's placement, with each level's code and name (null for levels deeper than the DLC's position). Joins to HR_ORG_UNIT and FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY; used to report or filter the master-hierarchy placement (school/area path) of a DLC, and as a DLC scope filter when only DLCs present in the standard hierarchy should be included.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_FLOOR\", \"desc\": \"Facilities floor snapshot table (FAC_* family): one row per floor of a building with floor number/label, gross, assignable and non-assignable areas, sort sequence, level, wing, and access level. Same floor structure as FCLT_FLOOR but keyed by FLOOR_KEY/BUILDING_KEY joining FAC_ROOMS.FLOOR_KEY and FAC_BUILDING.FAC_BUILDING_KEY; used as the floor source when FAC_* family keys are involved.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_HIST\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities building snapshot table: one row per building per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format, covering 201505-201906, 48 periods, ~255 buildings), preserving each building's attributes over time: identifiers and names, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, site, campus sector, access level, building type, ownership type, use, occupancy class, height, cost center/collector references, coordinates, and number of rooms. Used for fiscal-period building history analysis (area/room-count trends, dispersion statistics across historical records); use FCLT_BUILDING for the current snapshot. Date columns (DATE_BUILT/DATE_ACQUIRED/DATE_OCCUPIED) are stored in MM/DD/YYYY format; FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1 is the variant storing them in DD-MON-YY format.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_BUILDING_ADDRESS\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building address table (FAC_* family): one row per address record of a building (street, mail, parcel, E911 purposes), with street number/name/suffix, directionals, city, state, postal code, address purpose, and E911 flag. Same address structure as FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS but keyed by BUILDING_KEY joining FAC_BUILDING.FAC_BUILDING_KEY; used as the address source when FAC_* family keys are involved.\"}, {\"id\": \"BUILDINGS\", \"desc\": \"Space-domain building lookup table: one row per building with building key/number, building name, street and mailing addresses as single text fields, gross and assignable square footage (in square feet), and a building counter. Referenced by SPACE_DETAIL via BUILDING_KEY; a lightweight building reference for space-assignment reporting, without the type/ownership/site classification carried by FCLT_BUILDING or FAC_BUILDING.\"}, {\"id\": \"FUND_CENTER_HIERARCHY\", \"desc\": \"24 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW\", \"desc\": \"Newer HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with the same unit/department identity and hierarchy-path structure as HR_ORG_UNIT (unit key/ID/title/level, HR department code and name variants, school-area/top-level/root names, hierarchy path levels 1-5, DLC_KEY) but a shallower hierarchy path (levels 6-7 absent), no HR_DEPARTMENT_ID and no DLC_NAME column, and an extra HR_DEPARTMENT_ABBR abbreviation column. Holds more unit rows than HR_ORG_UNIT (691 vs 641, including units absent from HR_ORG_UNIT); use HR_ORG_UNIT when DLC_NAME or the deeper hierarchy path is required, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW for the newer unit coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"FRC_FISCAL_PERIODS\", \"desc\": \"3 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_FLOOR\", \"desc\": \"Space-domain floor lookup table: one row per floor key with the floor number/label and floor name. Referenced by SPACE_DETAIL via FLOOR_KEY to attach floor identity to assigned rooms; a lightweight floor reference without the area measures carried by FCLT_FLOOR or FAC_FLOOR.\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy link table: one row per association between a department/lab/center (DLC) and a linked administrative object, classified by link type (Standard Funds Center, PCMIT-0 Profit Center, New/Old Org. Unit, Facilities Org., Student Systems Unit, NIMBUS B.A.G.). A DLC may hold many links of several types. Joins to MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY; used to map DLCs to their fund centers, profit centers, facilities organizations, and other linked object codes.\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT\", \"desc\": \"Department parent lookup table: one row per department code (D_CODE) with its department name and the identity of its direct parent department (parent ID, parent D code, parent name). A flattened single-level parent view of the department tree; use MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY when the full multi-level hierarchy path of a DLC is required. D_CODE matches MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY/DLC_CODE and other DLC key columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"DRUPAL_EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY\", \"desc\": \"Drupal-sourced employee directory table: an alternative employee feed keyed by MIT_ID with name components, employee group/type, additional/dual appointment flags, office location and phone, HR organization unit id/title, directory/primary titles, email address, and personal URL. Same person domain as EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY but from the Drupal source system and without Kerberos/preferred-name columns; used as an alternative employee lookup when Drupal-sourced attributes (employee group, appointment flags, HR org unit) are needed.\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_FACULTY_ROSTER\", \"desc\": \"HR faculty roster table: one row per faculty member keyed by MIT_ID with name components, terminal degree, appointment type, job/position titles across HR, administrative, and directory organization units, endowed chair, and emeritus status. Used for faculty appointment and credential analysis; joins to EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY on MIT_ID for contact details.\"}, {\"id\": \"MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Moira mailing-list/group membership detail table: one row per list member with the list key, list owner key, member login, member full name, member MIT ID, last update date, and a counter. Used to find which Moira lists a person belongs to (joining EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY on MOIRA_LIST_MEMBER_MIT_ID = MIT_ID), and to decode list identity via MOIRA_LIST and ownership via MOIRA_LIST_OWNER.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Section-level subject offering fact table: one row per subject section offered in a term, with section flags (master/lecture/lab/recitation/design), cluster information, offering department and school, responsible faculty, meeting time/place, and enrollment numbers at section, subject, and cluster level. Linked to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (subject level) via SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY/COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY and to SUBJECT_SUMMARY via SUBJECT_SUMMARY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"ROLES_FIN_PA\", \"desc\": \"2 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"TIME_QUARTER\", \"desc\": \"Quarter-level time dimension table: one row per fiscal quarter (FY_QUARTER_CODE such as 'FY2014Q1') covering fiscal years 2000-2035 (144 quarters), with fiscal and calendar quarter codes/names, fiscal and calendar years, quarter start/end dates, the quarter's start/end fiscal periods, payroll certification open/expected/due dates, current/next/previous/past/future quarter flags, and a payroll certification schedule key. Joins to TIME_MONTH via FY_QUARTER_CODE to roll months up to quarters; used for fiscal-quarter scheduling and certification-deadline reporting.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level rollup of section offerings per term: one row per subject offered in a term with unit structure (total/lecture/lab/preparation units), offering department and school, responsible faculty, cluster information, and enrollment numbers. Parent of SUBJECT_OFFERED (section level) via COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"SIS administrative department table with administrative department code/name, phone area code and phone number, and clearing cost collector. Joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT via SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE for department contact information.\"}, {\"id\": \"TOP_LEVEL_DOMAIN\", \"desc\": \"4 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD\", \"desc\": \"Space-planning room load table: one row per room record from the space planning feed, with the building-room identifier, building component, floor (numeric or label such as 'G9'), space usage text (e.g. 'DSGN STUDIO', 'CONF RM'), space unit code, HR organization unit id, and room access level. Links rooms to SPACE_UNIT via SPACE_UNIT_CODE and to FCLT_ORGANIZATION/HR_ORG_UNIT via HR_ORG_UNIT_ID; used for floor/access-level/space-usage room analysis from the space-planning perspective, without the area and use-key columns carried by FCLT_ROOMS.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Space assignment detail fact table: one row per physical room assigned to a space unit, with building/floor/space-unit/space-usage keys, room identifiers (building-room number and name, room number), room square footage, room counter, and building component. Used to count rooms per space unit or per building, and to analyze room size and usage distribution. Joins to SPACE_UNIT via SPACE_UNIT_KEY, FCLT_BUILDING via BUILDING_KEY, SPACE_FLOOR via FLOOR_KEY, and SPACE_USAGE via SPACE_USAGE_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_PERSON\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject person table: one row per person associated with an IAP activity, recording the person's role in the activity (Activity leader, Session leader, Contact person), MIT affiliation type, name, location, email, organization, and title. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_PERSON_KEY; used to analyze activity leadership and person roles, e.g. enrollment capacity statistics per person role.\"}, {\"id\": \"PROFIT_CENTER_GROUP\", \"desc\": \"24 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level summary fact table per term: one row per subject (or cluster) per term with department/school attribution, unit structure (total/lecture/lab/prep/design units), and detailed enrollment statistics including final enrollment, first-week and fifth-week enrollment, and credit/listener splits at both subject and cluster level. Used for enrollment and unit statistics by department, school, term, and subject group.\"}, {\"id\": \"IR_INSTITUTION\", \"desc\": \"13 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG\", \"desc\": \"Drupal-sourced course catalog table: an alternative catalog feed with the same subject attribute structure as COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (units, grading, requirement attributes, offering flags, section flags, meeting time/place), plus subject-offering reference columns (SO_SUBJECT_ID, SO_TERM_CODE, SO_TERM_DESCRIPTION, SO_CLUSTER_TYPE) linking catalog records to registrar subject offerings.\"}, {\"id\": \"EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY\", \"desc\": \"Employee directory table: one row per institute employee with MIT ID, legal and preferred name components, directory/primary titles, HR department number and name, office location and office phone, email address, personal URL, and Kerberos name. Used to resolve responsible faculty contact details (full name, email, office phone) for subject offerings via RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID = MIT_ID, and to link employees to Moira mailing list membership via MIT_ID = MOIRA_LIST_MEMBER_MIT_ID.\"}, {\"id\": \"binding_action_revisions\", \"desc\": \"18 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"MOIRA_LIST\", \"desc\": \"Moira mailing-list/group master table: one row per list with list key, name, description, active flag, and type flags (mailing list, group, NFS group, public, hidden). Parent of MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL via MOIRA_LIST_KEY.\"}], \"metric\": [{\"id\": \"dw_2559\", \"desc\": \"For each DLC whose DLC name contains the word 'Office', is not the biology department, and has at least one assignable organization, what are the DLC key, DLC name, the number of unique organizations, the total number of assignable organizations, the department name, the maximum organization number, the name of the space unit associated with that department, and the earliest warehouse load date among its organizations, considering only departments in the \\\"Provost Area\\\" with a maximum organization number greater than 50000 and excluding the \\\"Political Science\\\" department (Course 17)? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3153\", \"desc\": \"Among all organizations with a DLC key of 'D_MECHE' and an organization level of 5, what are the names and descriptions of these organizations, and for each, what is the name and description of their parent organization? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4562\", \"desc\": \"For each organization with an organization level of 5 whose space unit is among the top 10 space units by number of rooms, display the organization name, organization key, description, space unit, space unit key, the average organization key within each organization key group ordered by space unit key, the count of rooms for each space unit, and the building with the highest number of rooms in that space unit, along with the count of rooms in that building. Order the results by the count of rooms descending and then by space unit key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4330\", \"desc\": \"For each organization that is assignable and has a department code above 100000, and for which there exists a space unit with space unit code equal to 97500, show the organization key, organization name, department name, the number of HR org units, the total of their department IDs, the latest warehouse load date from HR_ORG_UNIT, the space unit name, the DLC name, the DLC key from the organization, the minimum space unit code in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the facility organization key, and the total number of space units per organization, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4627\", \"desc\": \"For organizations with an organization level of 5, show the organization name, organization ID, DLC name, HR org unit title, HR department name, HR org unit level, and assign row numbers within each HR department name group ordered by organization name. For each such organization, for each room with area greater than 200 and assignable major use that belongs to the organization, show the building room, floor, room number, space ID, area, major use name, major use description, and the minimum area value over each major use group. Additionally, for each such room, show the HR org unit title and HR org unit level from the HR_ORG_UNIT table (joined via DLC_KEY). Present the results with the columns: organization name, organization ID, DLC name, HR org unit title, HR department name, HR org unit level, row number, building room, floor, room number, space ID, area, major use name, major use description, minimum area per major use, HR org unit title (from HR_ORG_UNIT), and HR org unit level (from HR_ORG_UNIT), in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3890\", \"desc\": \"For each major use description, list the building-room identifier, area, major use description, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the major use description, as well as the organization name, department name, department code, department long name, department level, and the average organization number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the organization parent, ordered by the organization name, but only include those organizations whose organization number is greater than the average organization number of their parent group. For each major use description, include a grand total row for all rooms in the format of (null, null, major use description, total rooms) and only include rooms whose organization matches the filtered organizations. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4612\", \"desc\": \"For each organization whose parent is 'S H&SS' and that is associated with a space unit with space unit code 97500, list the organization name, description, HR org unit title, row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the organization name, the space unit name, space unit code, department count, number of supervisees, the average department count within each department count group ordered by number of supervisees, and the total square footage for each organization. Include subtotals for each organization (the corresponding organization name field is 'SUBTOTAL') and a grand total across all organizations (the corresponding organization name field is 'TOTAL'). Do not repeat the organization name if it is the same as the previous row. Sort the table by organization name and space unit name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3452\", \"desc\": \"For organizations with an organization level of 5 and departments in the \\\"Provost Area\\\" with a non-null department code, show the organization name, organization ID, DLC name, HR org unit title, HR department name, HR org unit level, the row number within each HR department name group ordered by organization name, the department's long name, the corresponding hierarchy level 3 name from the master department hierarchy, and the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the department name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4590\", \"desc\": \"For organizations with an organization level of 5, show the organization name, organization ID, DLC name, HR org unit title, HR department name, HR org unit level, and assign row numbers within each HR department name group ordered by organization name. For each such organization, for each room with area greater than 200 and assignable major use, show the building room, floor, room number, space ID, area, major use name, major use description, and the minimum area value over each major use group. Additionally, for each such room, show the HR org unit title and HR org unit level from the HR_ORG_UNIT table (joined via DLC_KEY), and the difference between the room's area and the minimum area for its major use. Order the results by HR department name, organization name, and major use. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3410\", \"desc\": \"For rooms with an area greater than 300 and located in buildings with more than 100 rooms, show the building's long name, the room's full name, the room's area, and the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the building's long name, along with the name of the space unit, the associated organization name, and both the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the organization numbers for all organizations linked to that space unit (considering only space units with a non-null DLC key and organizations with assignable status), where the room and the space unit share the same organization key. List the columns in the following order: building's long name, room's full name, room's area, window row number, space unit name, organization name, organization number variance, and organization number standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4025\", \"desc\": \"For rooms with a square footage of 150, show the space unit code, space unit name, and the maximum rank within each space unit code group, and for each of those space units, show the major organization, top-level HR organization name, HR department name, the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the organization numbers for each HR department name, considering only organizations that are assignable and have a non-null organization number. The results should include the space unit code, space unit name, maximum rank, major organization, top-level HR organization name, HR department name, average organization number, organization number variance, and organization number standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3692\", \"desc\": \"For each organization and department in the Provost Area with a non-null department code, where the organization level is 5 and assignable is 1, show the organization name, organization key, department name, department code, the average organization key within each organization key group ordered by department code, the department's long name, the corresponding hierarchy level 3 name from the master department hierarchy, and the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the department name. The columns should be shown in the following order: organization name, organization key, department name, department code, the average organization key window value, department's long name, hierarchy level 3 name, and the department hierarchy row number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3235\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and its corresponding facility organization key where the department is in the Provost Area, provide the number of organizations, the minimum department hierarchy level 3 code, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of HR organization units per facility organization (considering only those with a non-null DLC key and where the hierarchy type is 'Standard Hierarchy'), listing the results in order by department name and facility organization key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4773\", \"desc\": \"For each organization with an organization level of 5 and for rooms on floor 2 that are associated via space unit code, show the organization name, organization key, description, space unit, space unit key, the average organization key within each organization key group ordered by space unit key, the building room, space usage, the HR org unit title, the department name, the minimum access level in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the building component, and the HR org unit level and department code for each room, ordered by organization name and building room. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3332\", \"desc\": \"List all rooms that either have an area greater than 400 or are in buildings starting with 'E' and have area greater than 50. For each room, show the building room identifier, floor number, major use description, organization name, building name, building type, and the minimum floor number in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the building key (for rooms with area greater than 400); or show the building room identifier, room key, area, organization name, department code, DLC key, and the minimum area value over each DLC key group ordered by DLC key (for rooms in buildings starting with 'E' and area greater than 50). Indicate the source of each row as either 'AreaRooms' or 'E_BuildingRooms'. The columns are: building room identifier, floor number, major use description, organization name, building name, building type, minimum floor number in window, room key, area, department code, DLC key, minimum area in DLC window, and source. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1864\", \"desc\": \"For each organization whose organization level is 5 and is not 'ADMISSIONS', and for each organization and its corresponding HR department where the organization is assignable, the HR organization unit level is 'DEPARTMENTS', the organization is not 'Cambridge-MIT Institute', and the organization is in the 'Provost Area' top-level HR hierarchy, but excluding organizations with organization IDs '138' and '250', show the organization name, description, the corresponding space unit name, the total number of space units associated with each organization, the HR department name, the number of organizations, and the minimum organization number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1833\", \"desc\": \"For each department and subject grade type where the subject is offered in the current academic year, is letter graded, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the number of subjects, the minimum total units, the school name, the department phone number, the organization name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the areas of its rooms, and the department's DLC name, including subtotals for each department (the corresponding department field is 'SUBTOTAL') and a grand total across all departments (the corresponding department field is 'TOTAL'). Do not repeat the department if it is the same as the previous row. Only include organizations that have more than 5 rooms, are associated with a non-null DLC key, and are not the 'ADMISSIONS' department or the 'Political Science' department. Sort the table by department, grade type, and descending standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of room areas. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2591\", \"desc\": \"For all subjects in the 2014FA term with at least one enrolled student, show the subject title, offering department name, responsible faculty name, the TIP material status key, the total number of units, and the minimum total number of units in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the course number, along with the cluster type description and the HGN code description for each subject. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1465\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the Provost Area at the School of Science level, excluding the Biology department, and for each organization within those departments (excluding organizations with IDs '138' and '250'), show the department name, department code, organization name, organization ID, the maximum average organization number within each department code group, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the area of rooms assigned to the organization (considering only organizations with more than 5 rooms and excluding organizations named 'ADMISSIONS'), ordered by department name and organization name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2956\", \"desc\": \"For all active Moira lists that are also Moira mailing lists, show the list key, list name, whether the list is public, the member's full name, the member's MIT ID, the last update date, and the minimum MIT ID value over each list key group. Include subtotals for each list key (the corresponding list key field is 'SUBTOTAL') and a grand total across all lists (the corresponding list key field is 'TOTAL'). Do not repeat the list key if it is the same as the previous row. Sort the table by list key and list name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2901\", \"desc\": \"For each Moira list member whose last update date is '18-DEC-24', show the Moira list key, the member's full name, the owner's type, the member's MIT ID, the list owner, the last update date, and whether the member's MIT ID is above or below the average MIT ID for their owner type. If it's above, label as 'ABOVE_AVERAGE', if below, label as 'BELOW_AVERAGE', otherwise 'AVERAGE'. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3985\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the academic term with term code '2006FA' in departments that offer more than 5 subjects in that term, show the subject ID, subject title, department name, the sum of lecture units within each grade type group, and the total number of subjects per department for that term. Additionally, for each subject offered by the same department in the term '2017JA', show the number of enrolled students, offering department name, department full name, subject code, subject code description, and whether the number of enrolled students is 'HIGH_ENROLLMENT' (at least 10% greater than the average for that subject code), 'LOW_ENROLLMENT' (at least 10% less than the average for that subject code), or 'AVERAGE'. Present the results ordered by subject ID and subject code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3635\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units, and for subjects offered in the term 2019FA from the same department, show the subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, the rank of each 2024 subject within its department ordered by subject code, the 2019FA subject ID, number of enrolled students in 2019FA, department full name, and the row number of each 2019FA subject within its department name group ordered by subject ID. Order the results by department name, subject code, and 2019FA subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4452\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the \\\"Provost Area\\\" that is associated with a space unit with space unit code 97500, show the department code, department name, school area name, the rank of each department within its school area based on department code, the corresponding DLC name, the space unit name, space unit code, associated organization name, department count, number of supervisees, and the highest research volume ever recorded for each department count group. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4515\", \"desc\": \"For each department, academic year, activity title, and sponsor name where the subject enrollment number is greater than 10 and the maximum enrollment for the activity is greater than 10, provide the department name, academic year, number of unique subjects, minimum total units offered, activity title, sponsor name, number of unique activities, minimum fee, and the sponsor type. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3959\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term with code '2022FA' that also have at least one activity with an enrollment type of \\\"Advance sign-up required\\\" and a maximum enrollment of 12 (where the number of enrolled students is at least 10), show the subject ID, department name, subject term description, the running sum of total units within each academic year, subject title, whether the subject is offered in the fall term, the activity title, activity term code, activity maximum enrollment, activity term description, activity term start date, number of enrolled students in the activity, the offer department name for the activity, the responsible faculty name for the activity, and the row number of the activity within each subject title group, ordered by subject ID and activity title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3393\", \"desc\": \"For subjects with at least 5 enrolled students that are offered by the library in the term with code '2014FA', show the subject ID, subject title, number of enrolled students, term code, material status key, ISBN, row number within each material status group ordered by subject ID, offering department name, term description, term start date, term end date, and the minimum number of enrolled students for each offering department, ordered by offering department name, material status key, and subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3867\", \"desc\": \"For each subject in a department where the school code and subject title are not null, and for each subject offered in the 2022FA term with total units greater than the average for that term, display the subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, the number of subjects in the same department, the subject ID, the term description, and the running sum of total units for that academic year, ordered by subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3342\", \"desc\": \"For each space unit with a space unit key greater than 100000 that is associated with a department in the \\\"Provost Area\\\", show the space unit code, the organization name, the HR department name, the sum of space unit keys within each warehouse load date group, the HR department code, the school area name, and the rank of the department within its school area based on department code. Present the results ordered by school area name, department rank within school area, and space unit code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3911\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered by the library in the term with code '2014FA', show the subject ID, subject title, total number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, term start date, term end date, and the minimum number of enrolled students for each offering department, as well as the maximum windowed average record count from tip detail records with material status key 'RQ' (using a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by financial aid year). Additionally, for each offering department, include a grand total row showing the total number of enrolled students across all its subjects (with nulls for subject ID and subject title), and the corresponding maximum windowed average record count if available. Order the results by offering department name and subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3919\", \"desc\": \"For departments in the \\\"Sloan School of Management\\\" area with a hierarchy type of \\\"Standard Hierarchy\\\", show the department code, department name, the dense rank of each department considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the department's long name, and the corresponding DLC name from the MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY table, along with, for each such department, the space unit code, organization name, HR department name from the space unit, the sum of space unit keys within each warehouse load date group, and the HR org unit title for space units with a space unit key greater than 100000, where the department and space unit share the same DLC key. Present the results in the order of department code and space unit code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3916\", \"desc\": \"For each warehouse load date, list the space unit code, organization name, HR department name, the HR org unit title, the sum of space unit keys within each warehouse load date group (including a grand total row with nulls and the total sum), and for each, show the building room, space usage, space unit name, and the total number of rooms in the same space unit on floor 2 with access level 1 (only including space units with more than 1 such room), for space units with a space unit key greater than 100000. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4776\", \"desc\": \"For rooms with an area greater than 300 that are associated with departments in the \\\"Provost Area\\\", show the building-room identifier, floor number, major use description, organization name, DLC key, the average area in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by department code and ordered by area, the department code, department name, school area name, and the rank of each department within its school area based on department code. Additionally, include the department's full name from the HR organization unit and the department's hierarchy level 3 name from the master department hierarchy. Present the results ordered by building-room identifier and department code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1357\", \"desc\": \"For each access level code and campus sector, what is the access level code, access level name, campus sector, the variance of the number of rooms in the building history for buildings with a nonzero number of rooms, assignable area greater than 0, and that are residential buildings at MIT, as well as, for each floor in the Fairchild Building with access level 1 or 2 and in academic buildings, the floor number, the building's long name, the range and variance of the area of rooms on that floor? Only include buildings that are at MIT. Also, include subtotals for each access level code (the corresponding campus sector field is 'SUBTOTAL') and a grand total across all access level codes (the corresponding campus sector field is 'TOTAL'). Do not repeat the access level code if it is the same as the previous row. Sort the table by access level code, campus sector, and floor. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4271\", \"desc\": \"For rooms on floor 2 with access level 1, show the space unit, the maximum row number (within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by building room) for each space unit, the building room, the organization name, the department name, and the difference between the access level of the room and the average access level for that department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4033\", \"desc\": \"For rooms on floor 2, show the building room, space usage, the organization name, the HR org unit title, the department name, the minimum access level in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the building component, the department's long name, the DLC name, and the highest floor among rooms with access level 1 for each space usage group. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3861\", \"desc\": \"For subject offerings in the term '2017FA' with a total number of units greater than 10, display the subject title, department name, school name, and their dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the department code from the subject code table, along with any matching subject IDs from subjects offered in the term with code '2022SU', their department names, and their dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the total number of units. Show the subject title, department name, school name, subq1 dense rank, subject ID, subq2 department name, and subq2 dense rank, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2735\", \"desc\": \"For each fiscal year, what is the minimum calendar month and the sum of calendar years from TIME_MONTH for months that have at least one corresponding day in TIME_DAY with the academic term code '2020FA'? Show only fiscal years where such months exist. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_5103\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2017JA', show the subject title, the number of enrolled students, the responsible faculty name, the offering department name, the department full name, the school name, and the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the department code. Additionally, for subjects offered in the term with code '2022FA' in the same department, provide the subject ID, department name, term description, the running sum of total units within each academic year ordered by subject ID, and the subject's short title and responsible faculty name from the course catalog. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1758\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with total units equal to 12 in the Mathematics department, show the department code, department name, subject code, subject number, subject title, total units, the row number within each department ordered by subject code, the deviation of each subject's total units from the average total units of all Mathematics subjects offered in 2024, the number of enrolled students, responsible faculty name, school name, and the dense rank over the department name ordered by department name for those subjects that also have course materials and were offered in the term '2019FA'. Sort the table by department name and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_100\", \"desc\": \"Among all departments, which are the top 5 departments with the highest average office phone number among graduate students (student year 'G') who have a non-null office phone number? For each of these departments, show the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of office phone numbers, and the full name and office phone number of the graduate student in that department with the highest office phone number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4308\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2017JA', show the subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, department full name, subject code, subject code description, and the minimum number of enrolled students over each subject code group, as well as the school code, school name, department code, school name from department, department phone number, and the highest running sum of total units for any subject within that school in the 2019FA term (where the subject has more than 1 total unit). Order the results by subject code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3684\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term with code '2025FA' by departments in the School of Engineering, show the subject ID, subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, term start date, term end date, term parameter, the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department, total units, department full name, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title, ordered by offering department name and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3490\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the \\\"Provost Area\\\" with a non-null department code, show the department name, the department's long name, the corresponding hierarchy level 3 name from the master department hierarchy, the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the department name, and for each matching space unit with a space unit key greater than 100000, show the space unit code, the organization name, the HR department name from the space unit, and the sum of space unit keys within each warehouse load date group ordered by space unit key. Present the results ordered by department name and space unit code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3277\", \"desc\": \"List all subject titles that are either (a) offered in the term '2022FA' with a total of 12 units, showing the subject title, department name from the course description, and the dense rank of each subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the subject code from the course catalog, or (b) for each subject offered, show the subject title, subject ID, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject key. The results should include all these columns in the following order: subject title, department name, window column, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and maximum number of enrolled students, with NULLs for columns not relevant to each case. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3944\", \"desc\": \"For each subject that is both offered in the academic term with term code '2006FA' and is in the \\\"Engineering\\\" school with total units equal to 1, show the subject ID, subject title, department name, the sum of lecture units within each grade type group ordered by subject ID, the name of the responsible faculty member for each subject, the academic year, the rank of each subject within its academic year group ordered by subject ID, the term description, and the term start date, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3224\", \"desc\": \"List all subjects from the term \\\"2010FA\\\" and all subjects offered in the term with code \\\"2025FA\\\", showing for each row: subject ID, term description, material status key, academic year, rank of the subject within each academic year group ordered by subject ID, subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term start date, term end date, term parameter, the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department, and the source term (\\\"2010FA\\\" or \\\"2025FA\\\"). The columns should appear in the following order: subject ID, term description, material status key, academic year, rank, subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term start date, term end date, term parameter, minimum enrolled students per department, and source term. Order the results by subject ID and source term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3482\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the 2012SU term that have a total of 1 unit and also have a cluster type of 'S', show the subject title from the summary, the course number from the offered table, the subject title from the offered summary, the department name from the summary, the offer department name from the offered summary, the row number within each department name group ordered by subject title from the summary, the subject title from SUBJECT_OFFERED, the offer department name from SUBJECT_OFFERED, the total units from SUBJECT_SUMMARY, and the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the subject title from SUBJECT_OFFERED. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_565\", \"desc\": \"For each academic building at MIT with building numbers between '14' and 'E62' or floor numbers at least 2, and floor numbers between 3 and 16, what are the minimum building number, average floor number, and the street name and city of the building's address? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2896\", \"desc\": \"For each facility organization, show the research volume, department names, square footage, MIT ID, and the average square footage in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows (grouped by facility organization key and ordered by research volume) for space supervisor usage records where the number of supervisees is 2, and only include those records where the average square footage in the window is greater than 200. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}], \"concept\": [{\"id\": \"concept_facility_organization_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Organization dimension tables describing the institute's hierarchical organization tree used for facilities/space attribution: FCLT_ORGANIZATION (keyed by FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, with DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME) and FAC_ORGANIZATION (keyed by ORGANIZATION_KEY, with D_CODE). They answer the same questions about organization names, hierarchy levels, parent/major organizations, assignable flags, and HR cross-references, but belong to different table families and coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_building_address\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the postal/street addresses of buildings: the current FCLT_* family address table (multiple purpose-typed address rows per building), its fiscal-period historical counterpart, the FAC_* family address snapshot, and the single-text address fields of the space-domain BUILDINGS lookup. They jointly answer questions about where a building is located (street number/name, city, state, postal code), but differ in time coverage, address decomposition, and table family.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_space_unit_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Space unit lookup tables identifying the organizational units that receive space allocation: SPACE_UNIT (with FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY organization attribution) and SPACE_UNIT2 (identity/name only). They answer the same space-unit identity questions but differ in organization linkage and coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_floor_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the floor level of buildings: the current FCLT_* family floor inventory with floor areas, the FAC_* family floor snapshot with the same structure, the fiscal-period historical floor table, and the lightweight space-domain floor lookup. They jointly answer questions about floor numbers and per-floor assignable/non-assignable areas, but differ in time coverage, table family, and attribute richness.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_dept_hr_org_hierarchy\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing the institute's department/lab/center (DLC) and HR organization hierarchies: the HR organization unit dimension in two feed variants (HR_ORG_UNIT, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW), the master department standard hierarchy path (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY), its DLC-to-administrative-object link table (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS), and the direct-parent department lookup (MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT). They jointly answer questions about which HR department/area a DLC or organization belongs to, the hierarchy path or parent of a department, and HR department names/codes/levels, and are joined to FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY for facilities/space attribution. They differ in hierarchy representation (full path vs direct parent vs HR unit attributes), unit coverage, and companion columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_building_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical building inventory and its attributes (number/name, type, ownership, site, campus sector, access level, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates): the current FCLT_* family snapshot, its fiscal-period history (in two date-format variants), the FAC_* family snapshot, and the lightweight space-domain building lookup. They jointly answer questions about building characteristics, areas, and room counts, but differ in time coverage, table family, attribute richness, and area units.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_room_major_use_classification\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables classifying rooms by major use (classrooms, offices, laboratories, residential, circulation, etc.) with a short code, description, and assignable-space flag. They cover the current classification in the FCLT and FAC table families and the fiscal-period historical classification in the FCLT family, jointly answering questions about what a room is primarily used for and whether that use counts as assignable space.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_room_space_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical room inventory and its space assignment: SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to space units with usage classification and square footage), FCLT_ROOMS (facilities room inventory with use classifications, organization assignment, and area in square meters), FAC_ROOMS (the FAC_* family room snapshot with the same structure as FCLT_ROOMS but FAC_* keys), and ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD (space-planning room load feed with floor, space usage text, access level, and space unit code / HR org unit id links). They jointly answer questions about how many rooms exist, room sizes, room usage, and which organization/space unit occupies rooms, but differ in assignment perspective, key family, and area units.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_person_directory\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing people of the institute keyed by MIT_ID: the primary employee directory (contact details, titles, HR department), the Drupal-sourced employee feed (employee group/type, appointment flags, HR org unit), the person master table (payroll rank, position title, active flag), the HR faculty roster (appointment type, terminal degree, emeritus status), the OPA current-person snapshot (HR job/appointment attributes, faculty flag, sabbatical), and the student directory (students with department attribution and student year). They jointly answer questions about who a person is, their contact details, job/appointment attributes, and whether they are employee, faculty, or student; responsible faculty in subject offering tables resolve to these tables via RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID = MIT_ID.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_moira_mailing_lists\", \"desc\": \"Tables of the Moira mailing-list/group domain: the list master (one row per list with name, description, active flag, and type flags such as mailing list, group, NFS group, public, hidden), the membership detail (one row per list member with member login, full name, MIT ID, and last update date), and the owner lookup (one row per owner entity with owner name and owner type LIST/USER/KERBEROS). They jointly answer questions about which lists exist and their properties, who belongs to a list, and who owns a list; MOIRA_LIST is the parent of MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL via MOIRA_LIST_KEY, and MOIRA_LIST_OWNER is referenced by MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL via MOIRA_LIST_OWNER_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_time_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Time dimension tables of the warehouse at three granularities: TIME_DAY (one row per calendar date, with fiscal/calendar year and period, academic year, financial aid year, day of week, and the academic term code/description of the day), TIME_MONTH (one row per fiscal period in YYYYMM format, covering fiscal years 1996-2035, with fiscal quarter, calendar month, academic term, and financial aid year mappings), and TIME_QUARTER (one row per fiscal quarter, covering fiscal years 2000-2035, with quarter dates, payroll certification deadlines, and quarter status flags). They jointly answer questions about when fiscal periods/quarters/days run, which fiscal/calendar/academic year a date or month belongs to, and how day-level records roll up to months and quarters. They link to each other via FISCAL_PERIOD (day-month), FY_QUARTER_CODE (month-quarter), and FISCAL_YEAR (month-quarter association within the same fiscal year, fanning out months across all quarters of the year), and to the academic term tables via TIME_DAY.ACADEMIC_TERM_CODE or TIME_MONTH.ACADEMIC_TERM = TERM_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_catalog_sources\", \"desc\": \"Tables providing catalog-level subject attributes (titles, unit structure, grading rules, HGN level, requirement attributes, offering-term flags) from different source systems: the warehouse course catalog, the CIS course catalog feed, and the Drupal course catalog feed. They answer the same catalog-attribute questions but differ in source system, extra columns, and join paths to department/subject-code lookups.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_subject_offering_facts\", \"desc\": \"Fact tables recording subjects offered per term from different business processes: the course catalog (planned catalog attributes), the registrar's section/subject offering records (actual sections and enrollment), subject-level summaries (final enrollment statistics), the textbook information program (subjects tracked for course materials), and library reserve processing (subjects with library reserve activity). They share subject identity (SUBJECT_ID, TERM_CODE) and department attribution but differ in granularity, enrollment semantics, and available measures.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_department_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables describing academic departments and their school attribution: the SIS department dimension, the student-facing department lookup, and the SIS administrative department (contact information). They answer questions about department names, full names, school code/name, degree-granting status, budget codes, and department phone numbers, but differ in attribute coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_cip_program_classification\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables of the Classification of Instructional Programs (CIP) used to classify courses/instructional programs into two-digit categories, four-digit series, and six-digit program codes, with revision version years (1990/2000/2010/2020). CIP holds the current single-version classification (one row per program code, with a change NOTE), while CIP_WITH_VERSION preserves every revision of each program code across versions. Both join to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION via PROGRAM_CODE = CIP_PROGRAM_CODE to attribute courses to CIP programs and categories.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_iap_activities\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing Independent Activities Period (IAP) activities offered in January terms: activity details (title, enrollment type, max enrollment, fee, cancellation flags), sessions (location, date, times), sponsors (name, type), categories, and persons. They jointly answer questions about IAP activity counts, enrollment capacity, fees, session scheduling, and sponsorship.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_material_programs\", \"desc\": \"Tables covering course material provisioning: the Textbook Information Program (TIP) tracking textbook adoption status per subject offering, and library reserve processing tracking catalog items placed on reserve for subjects. They jointly answer questions about which subjects have course materials/textbooks, material status (TIP statuses such as 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options; library statuses such as 'U' Unknown, 'Y' Required Course Material), ISBNs, record counts, and reserve catalog item attributes. The two programs are linked by SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_academic_term_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing academic terms and their calendar/status attributes. They jointly answer questions about when terms run, which academic/financial-aid/degree year a term belongs to, and whether a term is current, previous, future, or regular. Coverage differs: the full historical term list, the status-tracked term subset, and the three-row relative term parameter reference.\"}], \"column_concept\": [{\"id\": \"column_concept_facility_organization_key\", \"desc\": \"Facility organization key columns attributing space units and rooms to organizations in the hierarchical organization tree. Two naming conventions exist across table families (FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY in FCLT_*/SPACE_* tables vs ORGANIZATION_KEY in FAC_* tables) with the same value domain.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_dlc_key\", \"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key columns (values like 'D_AEROASTRO', 'D_IDSS', 'D_BIOLOGY') identifying a DLC across the facilities, HR, space, and academic-department domains. They are the universal cross-domain join key linking facilities organizations and space units to HR organization units, the master department hierarchy, and academic departments. Naming and completeness vary: DLC_KEY in most tables, D_CODE in MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT, DLC_CODE in the master hierarchy tables; some columns carry composite values ('D_DSL:HQ') or nulls.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_assignable_area\", \"desc\": \"Assignable-area measure columns at different granularity levels and time semantics: building-level current and per-fiscal-period assignable area, floor-level assignable area, and the space-domain assignable square footage. All FCLT_*/FAC_* columns are in square meters; BUILDINGS.BLDG_ASSIGNABLE_SQUARE_FOOTAGE is in square feet. Choosing the right column determines whether the measure is a building total, a floor total, a historical value, or a space-assignment figure.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_office_location\", \"desc\": \"OFFICE_LOCATION columns recording where a person's office/desk is, replicated across the person-directory tables (SE_PERSON, MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY, EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY, DRUPAL_EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY). All hold a building or building-room text identifier in the same value domain as FCLT_ROOMS.BUILDING_ROOM, but they describe different populations (employee/person master vs student vs primary employee directory vs Drupal employee feed) and differ sharply in non-null coverage and in how many values are building-room ('BLDG-ROOM') versus building-only ('BLDG'). Choosing the right column determines whose office is reported and whether room-level joins to FCLT_ROOMS succeed.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_fiscal_period\", \"desc\": \"Fiscal period code columns in YYYYMM format (e.g. '199602' = FY1996 period 2, '201505') appearing in two distinct roles: as the primary key of the month-grain time dimension (TIME_MONTH.FISCAL_PERIOD, also mirrored in TIME_DAY.FISCAL_PERIOD for day-to-month linkage), and as the snapshot-period stamp of the facilities historical tables (FCLT_BUILDING_HIST, FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1, FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS_HIST, FCLT_FLOOR_HIST, FCLT_ROOMS_HIST, FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST). Both roles share the same YYYYMM value domain, but the time dimension uses it for calendar grouping while the history tables use it to mark when a facilities snapshot was taken.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_access_level\", \"desc\": \"Access level columns recorded at three granularity levels of the facilities domain plus the space-planning room feed: building-level ACCESS_LEVEL_CODE/ACCESS_LEVEL_NAME (current and per-fiscal-period history), floor-level ACCESS_LEVEL, and room-level ACCESS_LEVEL (FCLT_ROOMS, FAC_ROOMS, ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD). They share a numeric value domain (observed 0-3) but describe the access restriction of different physical objects or come from different feeds, so filters and joins must target the granularity and table family the question refers to.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_master_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Master subject identifier columns (MASTER_SUBJECT_ID and its sortable variant MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT) replicated across the registrar offering tables, the subject summary, the textbook program, the library reserve program, and the CIS course catalog. For clustered subjects (e.g. joint or cross-listed offerings), the master subject identifier points to the leading subject of the cluster, so joining on it matches offerings that share the same master subject even when their own SUBJECT_ID differs. SUBJECT_ID/SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the subject itself, while MASTER_SUBJECT_ID/MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the cluster's master; the _SORT columns are the sortable forms of the same values used for cross-table joins.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_space_unit_key\", \"desc\": \"Space unit key columns identifying the organizational space-assignment unit across the space dimension and fact tables. SPACE_UNIT_KEY is the join key linking SPACE_DETAIL room rows to space unit identity (name/code) and, through SPACE_UNIT, to the owning facilities organization.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Subject identifier columns shared across catalog, registrar, textbook-program, and library tables. SUBJECT_ID is the cross-domain subject join key in 'CODE.NUMBER' format (e.g. '18.01'); it appears in every subject-related fact table but at different grains and program scopes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_term_code\", \"desc\": \"Term code columns in YYYYTT format (e.g. '2025FA', '2019SP', '2021JA', '2012SU'; TT = FA Fall, SP Spring, JA January/IAP, SU Summer) appearing across term dimension and fact tables. They are the universal join key linking subject offerings, textbook materials, library reserves, and IAP activities to term attributes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_num_of_rooms\", \"desc\": \"NUM_OF_ROOMS columns recording how many rooms a building contains, replicated across the current and historical building tables of both families. The building-table columns hold the current room count (one value per building); the history-table columns hold the room count at each fiscal period, used for room-count statistics (average, range, variance, minimum) across a building's history records.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_department_name\", \"desc\": \"Department name columns across subject offering, catalog, lookup, employee, and library reserve instructor tables. Two academic naming conventions exist (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME) with the same academic value domain; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT also holds academic departments but in a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME shares the column name but holds the HR organizational unit name (different value domain). Choosing the right one depends on the table family, the value format, whether the department is the catalog owner or the actual offering department, and whether an academic or HR department is meant.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_total_units\", \"desc\": \"Total credit unit columns replicated across catalog and registrar subject tables. They represent the same business quantity (total credit units of a subject) but come from different processes and pair with different companion unit columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_type_site\", \"desc\": \"Building classification columns replicated across the current and historical building tables of both table families: BUILDING_TYPE ('ACADEMIC', 'SERVICE', 'RESIDENT') and SITE ('MIT', 'BATES', 'LINC', 'BOS', etc.). They carry the same value domain but differ in time semantics: the building-table columns are the current classification, while the history-table columns are the classification recorded at each fiscal period, so filtering by one versus the other can select different building sets.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_year_columns\", \"desc\": \"Year columns across term, catalog, and time dimension tables representing different year systems: academic year, fiscal year, financial aid year, and degree year. Selecting the correct year system is essential for yearly grouping and partitioning.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_room\", \"desc\": \"Combined building-room identifier columns (e.g. '1-080') appearing in both the space assignment fact table and the facilities room inventory. They identify the same physical room concept but come from different business processes with different coverage and companion measures.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_enrollment_measures\", \"desc\": \"Enrollment measure columns across subject offering, summary, textbook-program, and library tables. Two families exist: NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (student headcount snapshots) and SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (official registrar enrollment), at section, subject, or program scope.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_material_status_key\", \"desc\": \"Material status key columns of the textbook program (TIP) and library reserve program. Both are coded status references decoded by their own lookup tables (key value equals code value), with independent value domains: TIP statuses ('RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options, 'RC' Recommended, 'PC' Val-u option, 'BR' Bookstore recommends, 'CL' Go to class first, 'NM' Course has no materials, 'U' Unknown, plus NULL-description keys) vs library reserve statuses ('U' Unknown, 'R' null description, 'N' Non-Required Course Material, 'O' Reserve only, 'X' No Required Textbook, 'Y' Required Course Material).\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_hass_attribute\", \"desc\": \"HASS (Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences) attribute code and description columns. The code columns appear in the three course catalog feeds and in the CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE lookup; description columns exist in three variants: the catalog-embedded HASS_ATTRIBUTE_DESC, the lookup's DESCRIPTION_ON_FORM (registration-form wording), and DESCRIPTION_IN_BULLETIN (short bulletin wording). Selecting the right description variant depends on the wording requested by the question.\"}]}}"
    },
    {
