    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_1e75e3b899554fdb99fbb679",
      "name": "semantic_get",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"entities\": [{\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"name\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy table: one row per department/lab/center (DLC) under the 'Standard Hierarchy' hierarchy type, recording the DLC key/code/name and its five-level hierarchy path from the institute root (level 1 'All Departments') through executive areas down to the DLC's placement, with each level's code and name (null for levels deeper than the DLC's position). Joins to HR_ORG_UNIT and FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY; used to report or filter the master-hierarchy placement (school/area path) of a DLC, and as a DLC scope filter when only DLCs present in the standard hierarchy should be included.\", \"columns\": {\"HIERARCHY_TYPE\": {\"desc\": \"Hierarchy classification of the row; only 'Standard Hierarchy' exists in current data\"}, \"DLC_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key, e.g. 'D_CAMPLAN'; joins to HR_ORG_UNIT.DLC_KEY and FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY\"}, \"DLC_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center code (same value as DLC_KEY in current data); matches MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT.D_CODE\"}, \"DLC_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center full name, e.g. 'Campus Planning'\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_1_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Code of the level-1 hierarchy node, 'D_ALL' for all rows\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_1_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the level-1 hierarchy node, 'All Departments'\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Code of the level-2 hierarchy node, e.g. 'D_EXECVP_AREA'\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the level-2 hierarchy node, e.g. \\\"Executive Vice President's Area\\\"\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_3_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Code of the level-3 hierarchy node; null when the DLC's path is shallower than 3 levels\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_3_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the level-3 hierarchy node, e.g. 'VP Finance Area'; null for shallow paths\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_4_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Code of the level-4 hierarchy node; null for shallow paths\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_4_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the level-4 hierarchy node; null for shallow paths\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_5_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Code of the level-5 (deepest) hierarchy node; null for shallow paths\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_5_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the level-5 (deepest) hierarchy node; null for shallow paths\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per DLC under the standard hierarchy type\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\", \"name\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization dimension table: one row per organization in the institute's hierarchical organization tree (levels 1-6, from institute-wide down to sub-units), with organization identifiers and names, parent and major-organization attribution, hierarchy level, assignable-space flag, course number for academic departments, description, DLC (department/lab/center) key and name, and cross-references to HR organization units. Parent of SPACE_UNIT (space assigned to organizations) and referenced by FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY for room occupancy attribution.\", \"columns\": {\"FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Surrogate key of the facilities organization; joins to SPACE_UNIT.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY and FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY\"}, \"ORGANIZATION_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Organization identifier (same value as the organization key in current data)\"}, \"ORGANIZATION\": {\"desc\": \"Short organization abbreviation, e.g. 'AERO', 'ADMISS'\"}, \"ORGANIZATION_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Display name of the organization, e.g. 'AERO & ASTRO'; used for organization-name reporting\"}, \"FCLT_ORG_PARENT_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Key of the parent organization in the hierarchy tree; null for the top-level organization\"}, \"ORG_PARENT\": {\"desc\": \"Abbreviation of the parent organization, e.g. 'S ENG' (School of Engineering)\"}, \"FCLT_MAJOR_ORG_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Key of the major (top-level grouping) organization this organization rolls up to\"}, \"MAJOR_ORG\": {\"desc\": \"Abbreviation of the major organization, e.g. 'PROVST', 'CHNCLR'\"}, \"ORGANIZATION_LEVEL\": {\"desc\": \"Level of the organization in the hierarchy tree (1 = institute-wide root, 2-4 = intermediate divisions/schools, 5 = department/DLC level, 6 = sub-organization); stored as string, filter with values like '5'\"}, \"ORGANIZATION_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Official organization number used in administrative systems\"}, \"ORGANIZATION_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable hierarchical organization code reflecting the tree path\"}, \"ASSIGNABLE\": {\"desc\": \"Flag ('1'/'0') indicating whether the organization is an assignable-space organizational unit\"}, \"COURSE\": {\"desc\": \"Academic course (department) number for degree-granting academic departments, e.g. '16' for Aeronautics and Astronautics; null for non-academic organizations\"}, \"DESCRIPTION\": {\"desc\": \"Long description of the organization, e.g. 'Department of Aeronautics and Astronautics'; null for many non-academic organizations\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}, \"DLC_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key, e.g. 'D_AEROASTRO'; joins to FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY.DLC_KEY, HR_ORG_UNIT.DLC_KEY (for HR org unit title/level and HR department attributes; may fan out when a DLC maps to multiple HR org units), and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY (for the standard department hierarchy path)\"}, \"DLC_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center full name, e.g. 'Aeronautics and Astronautics'\"}, \"HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE_OLD\": {\"desc\": \"Legacy HR department code cross-reference\"}, \"HR_ORG_UNIT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"HR organization unit identifier cross-reference; links to HR_ORG_UNIT\"}, \"HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Department name as recorded in HR systems\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per facilities organization\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1864\", \"name\": \"Level-5 Assignable Organization Space Units with Provost Area HR Department Statistics\", \"desc\": \"For each organization whose organization level is 5 and is not 'ADMISSIONS', and for each organization and its corresponding HR department where the organization is assignable, the HR organization unit level is 'DEPARTMENTS', the organization is not 'Cambridge-MIT Institute', and the organization is in the 'Provost Area' top-level HR hierarchy, but excluding organizations with organization IDs '138' and '250', show the organization name, description, the corresponding space unit name, the total number of space units associated with each organization, the HR department name, the number of organizations, and the minimum organization number. Do not return any rounded answers.\", \"sql\": \"WITH org_space_units AS ( SELECT ORGANIZATION_NAME, DESCRIPTION, SPACE_UNIT, COUNT(SPACE_UNIT) OVER (PARTITION BY ORGANIZATION_NAME) AS total_space_units, DLC_KEY FROM ( SELECT t0.ORGANIZATION_NAME, t0.DESCRIPTION, t1.SPACE_UNIT, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY t1.SPACE_UNIT ROWS BETWEEN 2 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING) AS window_column, t0.DLC_KEY FROM FCLT_ORGANIZATION t0 JOIN SPACE_UNIT t1 ON t0.DLC_KEY = t1.DLC_KEY WHERE t0.ORGANIZATION_LEVEL = 5 AND t0.ORGANIZATION_NAME <> 'ADMISSIONS' AND t0.ORGANIZATION_ID NOT IN ('138', '250') ) inner_cte ), org_hr_dept AS ( SELECT ic.ORGANIZATION, ic.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME, ic.organization_count, ic.min_organization_number, f.DLC_KEY FROM ( SELECT f.ORGANIZATION, h.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME, COUNT(f.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY) AS organization_count, MIN(f.ORGANIZATION_NUMBER) AS min_organization_number FROM FCLT_ORGANIZATION f JOIN HR_ORG_UNIT h ON f.HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE_OLD = h.HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE_OLD WHERE f.ASSIGNABLE = 1 AND h.HR_ORG_UNIT_LEVEL = 'DEPARTMENTS' AND f.ORGANIZATION_NAME NOT IN ('CAMBRIDGE-MIT INST') AND f.ORGANIZATION_ID NOT IN ('138', '250') GROUP BY f.ORGANIZATION, h.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME ) ic JOIN HR_ORG_UNIT h2 ON ic.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME = h2.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME JOIN FCLT_ORGANIZATION f ON ic.ORGANIZATION = f.ORGANIZATION WHERE h2.ORG_HIER_TOP_LEVEL_NAME = 'Provost Area' ) SELECT osu.ORGANIZATION_NAME, osu.DESCRIPTION, osu.SPACE_UNIT, osu.total_space_units, ohd.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME, ohd.organization_count, ohd.min_organization_number FROM org_space_units osu JOIN org_hr_dept ohd ON osu.DLC_KEY = ohd.DLC_KEY;\", \"category\": \"Facility Space and Organization Hierarchy Comprehensive Analysis\", \"default_granularity\": \"one row per level-5 organization space unit matched with its Provost Area HR department statistics\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_facility_organization_dimension\", \"name\": \"Facility Organization Dimension\", \"desc\": \"Organization dimension tables describing the institute's hierarchical organization tree used for facilities/space attribution: FCLT_ORGANIZATION (keyed by FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, with DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME) and FAC_ORGANIZATION (keyed by ORGANIZATION_KEY, with D_CODE). They answer the same questions about organization names, hierarchy levels, parent/major organizations, assignable flags, and HR cross-references, but belong to different table families and coverage.\", \"tables\": [\"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\", \"FAC_ORGANIZATION\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Key family\", \"differences\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION uses FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY/FCLT_ORG_PARENT_KEY/FCLT_MAJOR_ORG_KEY and is referenced by SPACE_UNIT and FCLT_ROOMS; FAC_ORGANIZATION uses ORGANIZATION_KEY/ORG_PARENT_KEY/MAJOR_ORG_KEY and is referenced by FAC_ROOMS.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Coverage\", \"differences\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION holds more organizations (180 rows) than FAC_ORGANIZATION (169 rows); key values overlap almost entirely, so FCLT_ORGANIZATION is the broader dimension.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"DLC attribution columns\", \"differences\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION carries both DLC_KEY and DLC_NAME plus an HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME; FAC_ORGANIZATION carries only D_CODE (no DLC name column).\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Shared structure\", \"differences\": \"Both share ORGANIZATION_ID/ORGANIZATION/ORGANIZATION_NAME, ORGANIZATION_LEVEL (1-6, level 5 = department/DLC), ORGANIZATION_NUMBER, ORGANIZATION_SORT, ASSIGNABLE, COURSE, DESCRIPTION, and HR cross-reference columns.\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Organization level, name, description, or hierarchy questions linked to space units or FCLT rooms\": \"Use FCLT_ORGANIZATION: it joins SPACE_UNIT.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY and FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY and has the widest organization coverage.\", \"Organization questions inside the FAC_* family (FAC_ROOMS occupancy, FAC_BUILDING analysis)\": \"Use FAC_ORGANIZATION: FAC_ROOMS.ORGANIZATION_KEY references it directly.\", \"DLC name reporting for an organization\": \"Use FCLT_ORGANIZATION: it is the only one carrying DLC_NAME alongside DLC_KEY.\"}}, {\"id\": \"concept_dept_hr_org_hierarchy\", \"name\": \"Department and HR Organization Hierarchy\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing the institute's department/lab/center (DLC) and HR organization hierarchies: the HR organization unit dimension in two feed variants (HR_ORG_UNIT, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW), the master department standard hierarchy path (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY), its DLC-to-administrative-object link table (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS), and the direct-parent department lookup (MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT). They jointly answer questions about which HR department/area a DLC or organization belongs to, the hierarchy path or parent of a department, and HR department names/codes/levels, and are joined to FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY for facilities/space attribution. They differ in hierarchy representation (full path vs direct parent vs HR unit attributes), unit coverage, and companion columns.\", \"tables\": [\"HR_ORG_UNIT\", \"HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW\", \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS\", \"MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Granularity and business object\", \"detail\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT and HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW hold one row per HR organization unit (641 and 691 rows respectively); MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY holds one row per DLC (310 rows) with its 5-level standard hierarchy path; MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS holds one row per DLC-to-linked-object association (fund centers, profit centers, facilities orgs, org units); MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT holds one row per department code with only its direct parent.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Hierarchy representation\", \"detail\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT carries the HR hierarchy path levels 1-7 plus school-area/top-level/root names and a unit level classification (ALL MIT, TOP LEVEL, DEPARTMENTS, SUB DEPARTMENT, ORGANIZATION LEVEL, NON HIERARCHY ORG UNITS); HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW carries only levels 1-5; MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY carries the master standard-hierarchy path levels 1-5 by code and name; MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT carries no path, only the immediate parent code/name.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Coverage and feed differences\", \"detail\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW is the newer feed with more units (691 vs 641, including 50 units absent from HR_ORG_UNIT) but lacks HR_DEPARTMENT_ID, DLC_NAME, and hierarchy levels 6-7, and adds HR_DEPARTMENT_ABBR; HR_ORG_UNIT is required when DLC_NAME or the deeper path is needed. MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY covers only DLCs placed in the 'Standard Hierarchy'; MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT covers 340 department codes including some outside that hierarchy.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"DLC cross-reference columns\", \"detail\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT carries DLC_KEY and DLC_NAME (DLC_KEY null for 133 units, and one DLC_KEY may map to multiple HR unit rows); HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW carries only DLC_KEY (possibly composite like 'D_DSL:HQ'); MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS carry DLC_KEY/DLC_CODE as their primary DLC identity; MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT uses D_CODE/D_NAME naming for the same value domain.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Companion attributes\", \"detail\": \"Only the HR_ORG_UNIT tables carry HR department identifiers/codes (HR_ORG_UNIT_ID, HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE 'HR-NNNNNN', HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE_OLD) and department name variants (short/long/alpha) used for HR department reporting; only MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS carries linked administrative object keys/codes and link type classification.\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"HR org unit title, HR org unit level, HR department name/code/long name for a facilities organization or DLC\": \"Use HR_ORG_UNIT joined via DLC_KEY; it is the only table carrying DLC_NAME alongside the HR department attributes and the full levels 1-7 path.\", \"HR department attributes for units missing from the older feed, or when the newer unit coverage is required\": \"Use HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW; it holds 50 units absent from HR_ORG_UNIT but lacks DLC_NAME and hierarchy levels 6-7.\", \"School/area placement or full standard-hierarchy path of a DLC, or restricting analysis to DLCs in the standard hierarchy\": \"Use MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY (levels 1-5 codes and names per DLC).\", \"Fund center, profit center, facilities organization, or other administrative object linked to a DLC\": \"Use MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS filtered by LINK_TYPE_CODE (FC, PMIT, FORG, ORG2, ORGU, SIS, BAG).\", \"Direct parent department of a department code (single-level parent lookup)\": \"Use MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT (PARENT_D_CODE/PARENT_D_NAME); use MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY instead when the multi-level path is needed.\"}}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_dlc_key\", \"name\": \"DLC Key (Department/Lab/Center)\", \"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key columns (values like 'D_AEROASTRO', 'D_IDSS', 'D_BIOLOGY') identifying a DLC across the facilities, HR, space, and academic-department domains. They are the universal cross-domain join key linking facilities organizations and space units to HR organization units, the master department hierarchy, and academic departments. Naming and completeness vary: DLC_KEY in most tables, D_CODE in MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT, DLC_CODE in the master hierarchy tables; some columns carry composite values ('D_DSL:HQ') or nulls.\", \"columns\": [\"FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY\", \"FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY.DLC_KEY\", \"HR_ORG_UNIT.DLC_KEY\", \"HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW.DLC_KEY\", \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY\", \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS.DLC_KEY\", \"MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT.D_CODE\", \"SPACE_UNIT.DLC_KEY\", \"SPACE_UNIT2.DLC_KEY\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT.DLC_KEY\", \"SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE.DEPT_NAMES\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Naming convention\", \"detail\": \"DLC_KEY is used by FCLT_ORGANIZATION, FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY, HR_ORG_UNIT, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW, MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY, MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS, SPACE_UNIT, SPACE_UNIT2, and SIS_DEPARTMENT; MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT names the same value domain D_CODE (with PARENT_D_CODE for the parent); MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY/LINKS additionally carry DLC_CODE holding the same value as DLC_KEY; SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE names it DEPT_NAMES despite holding DLC key values, not department names.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Uniqueness and fan-out behavior\", \"detail\": \"In MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY the DLC_KEY is unique per DLC (one row per DLC); in HR_ORG_UNIT one DLC_KEY may appear on multiple HR org unit rows (join fans out); in FCLT_ORGANIZATION multiple organizations can share a DLC_KEY; in FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY it is an assignment bridge where non-null values mark organizations with a DLC assignment; in SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE multiple supervisors can share the same DEPT_NAMES value, so joining DEPT_NAMES = DLC_KEY fans out on both sides.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Nullability and value format\", \"detail\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT.DLC_KEY is null for units without a DLC assignment (133 of 641 rows); HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW.DLC_KEY and SPACE_UNIT.DLC_KEY may contain composite values like 'D_DSL:HQ' that do not match plain DLC keys; SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE.DEPT_NAMES holds a comma-separated list of DLC keys when DEPT_COUNT > 1 (e.g. 'D_IDSS,D_LIDS'), so only single-department rows match a plain DLC key join; SIS_DEPARTMENT.DLC_KEY is populated for all 122 department rows.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Companion name column\", \"detail\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION, HR_ORG_UNIT, and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY carry a DLC_NAME alongside the key; SPACE_UNIT/SPACE_UNIT2, FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW, SIS_DEPARTMENT, and SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE carry only the key, so DLC name reporting requires joining one of the name-carrying tables.\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Attaching HR department attributes (unit title, department name/code, level) to a facilities organization\": \"Join FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY = HR_ORG_UNIT.DLC_KEY; expect possible row fan-out when a DLC maps to multiple HR org units.\", \"Reporting the DLC name of an organization or space unit\": \"Use FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY (carries DLC_NAME) or join HR_ORG_UNIT/MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY for DLC_NAME; SPACE_UNIT/SPACE_UNIT2 keys alone have no name column.\", \"Restricting analysis to DLCs placed in the standard department hierarchy or reporting their hierarchy path\": \"Join on MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY; use MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT.D_CODE for the same value domain when only the direct parent is needed.\", \"Filtering organizations that have a DLC assignment before DLC-level room statistics\": \"Use FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY.DLC_KEY IS NOT NULL as the assignment filter, then join FCLT_ORGANIZATION.\", \"Linking an academic department to its facilities organization or HR unit\": \"Use SIS_DEPARTMENT.DLC_KEY = FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY (or HR_ORG_UNIT.DLC_KEY); all SIS_DEPARTMENT rows carry a DLC key.\", \"Attributing supervisor space-usage statistics (supervisees, square footage, research volume) to a DLC or space unit\": \"Join SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE.DEPT_NAMES = SPACE_UNIT.DLC_KEY (or another DLC_KEY column); despite its name, DEPT_NAMES holds DLC key values, and only single-department rows (DEPT_COUNT = 1) match a plain DLC key.\"}}], \"not_found\": []}"
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_1ad0c2b6c7aa43059f05778c",
      "name": "semantic_graph",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 9, \"items\": [{\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with unit key/ID/title, unit level classification (ALL MIT, TOP LEVEL, DEPARTMENTS, SUB DEPARTMENT, ORGANIZATION LEVEL, NON HIERARCHY ORG UNITS), HR department identifiers and name variants (short, long, alphabetical), organization hierarchy area names (school area, top level, root), the full HR hierarchy path levels 1-7 (each with ID, sort order, and name), and DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME cross-references to departments/labs/centers. Joined from FCLT_ORGANIZATION and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY to attach HR department attributes (title, level, department name, long name, hierarchy path) to facilities organizations and DLCs; a single DLC_KEY can map to multiple HR org unit rows, so joins via DLC_KEY may fan out.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT\", \"name\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy link table: one row per association between a department/lab/center (DLC) and a linked administrative object, classified by link type (Standard Funds Center, PCMIT-0 Profit Center, New/Old Org. Unit, Facilities Org., Student Systems Unit, NIMBUS B.A.G.). A DLC may hold many links of several types. Joins to MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY; used to map DLCs to their fund centers, profit centers, facilities organizations, and other linked object codes.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS\", \"name\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Department parent lookup table: one row per department code (D_CODE) with its department name and the identity of its direct parent department (parent ID, parent D code, parent name). A flattened single-level parent view of the department tree; use MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY when the full multi-level hierarchy path of a DLC is required. D_CODE matches MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY/DLC_CODE and other DLC key columns.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT\", \"name\": \"MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization dimension table: one row per organization in the institute's hierarchical organization tree (levels 1-6, from institute-wide down to sub-units), with organization identifiers and names, parent and major-organization attribution, hierarchy level, assignable-space flag, course number for academic departments, description, DLC (department/lab/center) key and name, and cross-references to HR organization units. Parent of SPACE_UNIT (space assigned to organizations) and referenced by FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY for room occupancy attribution.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\", \"name\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Bridge table mapping facilities organizations to their department/lab/center (DLC) keys: one row per organization-DLC key assignment. Used to filter organizations that have a non-null DLC key assignment before joining FCLT_ORGANIZATION (via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY or DLC_KEY) for DLC-level facility and room statistics.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY\", \"name\": \"FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy table: one row per department/lab/center (DLC) under the 'Standard Hierarchy' hierarchy type, recording the DLC key/code/name and its five-level hierarchy path from the institute root (level 1 'All Departments') through executive areas down to the DLC's placement, with each level's code and name (null for levels deeper than the DLC's position). Joins to HR_ORG_UNIT and FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY; used to report or filter the master-hierarchy placement (school/area path) of a DLC, and as a DLC scope filter when only DLCs present in the standard hierarchy should be included.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"name\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy table: one row per department/lab/center (DLC) under the 'Standard Hierarchy' hierarchy type, recording the DLC key/code/name and its five-level hierarchy path from the institute root (level 1 'All Departments') through executive areas down to the DLC's placement, with each level's code and name (null for levels deeper than the DLC's position). Joins to HR_ORG_UNIT and FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY; used to report or filter the master-hierarchy placement (school/area path) of a DLC, and as a DLC scope filter when only DLCs present in the standard hierarchy should be included.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"name\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing the institute's department/lab/center (DLC) and HR organization hierarchies: the HR organization unit dimension in two feed variants (HR_ORG_UNIT, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW), the master department standard hierarchy path (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY), its DLC-to-administrative-object link table (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS), and the direct-parent department lookup (MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT). They jointly answer questions about which HR department/area a DLC or organization belongs to, the hierarchy path or parent of a department, and HR department names/codes/levels, and are joined to FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY for facilities/space attribution. They differ in hierarchy representation (full path vs direct parent vs HR unit attributes), unit coverage, and companion columns.\", \"entity_type\": \"concept\", \"id\": \"concept_dept_hr_org_hierarchy\", \"name\": \"Department and HR Organization Hierarchy\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key columns (values like 'D_AEROASTRO', 'D_IDSS', 'D_BIOLOGY') identifying a DLC across the facilities, HR, space, and academic-department domains. They are the universal cross-domain join key linking facilities organizations and space units to HR organization units, the master department hierarchy, and academic departments. Naming and completeness vary: DLC_KEY in most tables, D_CODE in MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT, DLC_CODE in the master hierarchy tables; some columns carry composite values ('D_DSL:HQ') or nulls.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_dlc_key\", \"name\": \"DLC Key (Department/Lab/Center)\"}]}"
    },
