      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"table_id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"table_name\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"count\": 11, \"items\": [{\"metric_id\": \"dw_3890\", \"name\": \"Access-Level-1 Room Counts per Major Use with Grand Totals Matched with Above-Parent-Average Organization Number Windows\", \"category\": \"Facility Space and Organization Hierarchy Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each major use description, list the building-room identifier, area, major use description, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the major use description, as well as the organization name, department name, department code, department long name, department level, and the average organization number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the organization parent, ordered by the organization name, but only include those organizations whose organization number is greater than the average organization number of their parent group. For each major use description, include a grand total row for all rooms in the format of (null, null, major use description, total rooms) and only include rooms whose organization matches the filtered organizations. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1465\", \"name\": \"Provost Area School of Science Department Organizations with Max Average Organization Number and Room Area Stddev\", \"category\": \"Facility Space and Organization Hierarchy Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the Provost Area at the School of Science level, excluding the Biology department, and for each organization within those departments (excluding organizations with IDs '138' and '250'), show the department name, department code, organization name, organization ID, the maximum average organization number within each department code group, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the area of rooms assigned to the organization 