RCHY with HR_ORG_UNIT variants and link/parent tables; decision guide: \"School/area placement or full standard-hierarchy path of a DLC → use MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.\"\n\n**Column Concepts**\n- **column_concept_dlc_key**: DLC_KEY is the universal cross-domain join key; in MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY it is **unique per DLC (one row per DLC)** → joining FCLT_ORGANIZATION on it does **not** fan out the organization rows.\n\n## 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\n- Graph neighbors of MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY: outgoing `joins` edges to **FCLT_ORGANIZATION** and HR_ORG_UNIT; incoming joins from MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS, MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT, FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY; concept membership `concept_dept_hr_org_hierarchy`; column concept `column_concept_dlc_key`.\n- `metrics_by_table(MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY)`: 11 metrics, all in the \"Facility Space and Organization Hierarchy\" / \"Organization Hierarchy Analysis\" categories, all joining it to FCLT_ORGANIZATION or HR_ORG_UNIT via DLC_KEY.\n- dw_1864's SQL lineage: FCLT_ORGANIZATION + HR_ORG_UNIT + SPACE_UNIT — establishes the exact measure expressions reused here.\n\n## 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (organization dimension candidates)**\n\n| Dimension | FCLT_ORGANIZATION | FAC_ORGANIZATION |\n|---|---|---|\n| Key family | FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY; joins MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY (concept comparison) | ORGANIZATION_KEY; carries D_CODE, no DLC_KEY (concept comparison) |\n| Coverage | 180 rows, broader (concept comparison) | 169 rows, fewer organizations |\n| Required columns | ORGANIZATION_NAME, ORGANIZATION_ID, ORGANIZATION_NUMBER, ASSIGNABLE, FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, DLC_KEY all present (retrieved columns) | Cannot join MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY (no DLC_KEY column) |\n| Fan-out risk | MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY unique per DLC → no fan-out (column_concept_dlc_key) | n/a |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness**\n- Measure `COUNT(FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY)`: FCLT_ORGANIZATION **SUPPORTED** (hint + dw_1864 precedent); FAC_ORGANIZATION **NOT-SUPPORTED** (no DLC_KEY join path to MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY).\n- Grouping key `MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_NAME`: only MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY **SUPPORTED** (hint mapping; column definition retrieved).\n- Filters `ASSIGNABLE`, `ORGANIZATION_NAME <> 'ADMISSIONS'`, `ORGANIZATION_ID NOT IN ('138','250')`: **SUPPORTED** on FCLT_ORGANIZATION (columns exist; dw_1864 uses identical literals).\n- Measure `MIN(ORGANIZATION_NUMBER)`: **SUPPORTED** (column exists; dw_1864 precedent).\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring**\n- \"department hierarchy level 2 name\" → lexically matches `MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_NAME` exactly (hint confirms).\n- \"organization is assignable\" → `ASSIGNABLE = 1` ('1'/'0' flag per column definition; dw_1864 writes `ASSIGNABLE = 1`).\n- \"number of organizations\" → `COUNT(FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY)` per hint mapping and dw_1864 precedent.\n- \"minimum organization number\" → `MIN(ORGANIZATION_NUMBER)` per hint and precedent.\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence**\n- COUNT(FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY) + MIN(ORGANIZATION_NUMBER) with the same three filters: 1 precedent — dw_1864.\n- MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY↔FCLT_ORGANIZATION DLC_KEY join: 11 metrics on the table (dw_3692, dw_3452, dw_3235, dw_1465, dw_2559, dw_3890, dw_3342, dw_3490, dw_3919, dw_4452, dw_4776).\n\n## 4. Business Usage\n\nFCLT_ORGANIZATION is the central facilities organization dimension (parent of SPACE_UNIT, referenced by FCLT_ROOMS); MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY supplies the standard-hierarchy placement path of DLCs and is used as scope filter/path reporter in 11 organization-hierarchy metrics. The DLC_KEY join between them is the documented, precedented path for attaching hierarchy level names to organizations.\n\n## 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n- MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY — semantic_search ✓, semantic_get ✓, query_neighbors ✓, metrics_by_table ✓\n- FCLT_ORGANIZATION — semantic_search ✓, semantic_get ✓ (via batch), neighbors via MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY traversal ✓\n- FAC_ORGANIZATION — semantic_search ✓, compared via concept_facility_organization_dimension ✓\n- dw_1864 — semantic_search ✓, semantic_get (full SQL) ✓\n- concept_facility_organization_dimension, concept_dept_hr_org_hierarchy — semantic_get ✓\n- column_concept_dlc_key — semantic_get ✓\n- Other search hits (rooms/buildings/subjects/persons tables & metrics) — screened as unrelated to this organization-hierarchy aggregation task, except the MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY metric list reviewed via metrics_by_table ✓\n- Note: `mysql_query` returned \"Access denied\" for every attempt (including `SELECT 1`), so live-data verification was impossible; the query was constructed strictly from retrieved schema definitions and the dw_1864 precedent SQL.\n\n## 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns**: MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY (`MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_NAME`, join key `DLC_KEY`) + FCLT_ORGANIZATION (`ORGANIZATION_NAME` group key/output, `ASSIGNABLE`, `ORGANIZATION_ID`, `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY` count measure, `ORGANIZATION_NUMBER` min measure, `DLC_KEY` join key).\n\n**6b. SQL approach**: INNER JOIN on DLC_KEY; WHERE `ASSIGNABLE = 1 AND ORGANIZATION_NAME <> 'ADMISSIONS' AND ORGANIZATION_ID NOT IN ('138','250')`; GROUP BY the two name columns; SELECT exactly the four requested columns in order. No fan-out risk since MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY is unique per DLC.\n\n**6c. Reasons**:\n- *Data*: DLC_KEY unique on the hierarchy side → count/min computed over organization rows only; all required columns physically exist per retrieved definitions.\n- *Semantic-network*: documented join edge MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY→FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY; concept decision guides select both tables; column_concept_dlc_key confirms join semantics.\n- *Business*: dw_1864 precedent uses identical filter literals and measure expressions (`COUNT(FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY)`, `MIN(ORGANIZATION_NUMBER)`); 11 metrics use the same join pattern.\n\n**6d. Alternatives**: FAC_ORGANIZATION lacks DLC_KEY and cannot reach MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY — excluded on evidence. No tie remaining.\n\n**Final SQL** (submitted):\n\n```sql\nSELECT\n    T1.MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_NAME,\n    T2.ORGANIZATION_NAME,\n    COUNT(T2.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY) AS number_of_organizations,\n    MIN(T2.ORGANIZATION_NUMBER) AS minimum_organization_number\nFROM MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY T1\nJOIN FCLT_ORGANIZATION T2\n    ON T1.DLC_KEY = T2.DLC_KEY\nWHERE T2.ASSIGNABLE = 1\n  AND T2.ORGANIZATION_NAME <> 'ADMISSIONS'\n  AND T2.ORGANIZATION_ID NOT IN ('138', '250')\nGROUP BY T1.MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_NAME, T2.ORGANIZATION_NAME\n```",
